 Computer Vision (interpreting images/video), and Robotics (autonomous physical actions).\n• **Modern AI**: Driven by deep neural networks, Large Language Models (LLMs), and Small Language Models (SLMs) that power intelligent assistants, recommendation engines, and autonomous systems.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(45,21,'USER','Explain Machine Learning with examples.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(46,21,'AI','**Machine Learning (ML)** is a subset of Artificial Intelligence where algorithms learn patterns from data and improve their performance over time without being explicitly programmed.\n\n• **Supervised Learning**: The model trains on labeled data.\n  *Example*: Spam detection where emails are labeled \'Spam\' or \'Inbox\'; house price prediction based on size and location.\n• **Unsupervised Learning**: The model discovers hidden patterns in unlabeled data.\n  *Example*: Customer segmentation for marketing; anomaly detection in credit card transactions.\n• **Reinforcement Learning**: An agent learns optimal actions through trial, errors, rewards, and penalties.\n  *Example*: Autonomous self-driving navigation; game-playing agents like AlphaGo.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(47,22,'USER','What is Python?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(48,22,'AI','**Python** is a high-level, interpreted, dynamically-typed programming language renowned for its clean syntax, readability, and versatile standard library.\n\n• **Key Characteristics**: Easy to learn, cross-platform, supports object-oriented, functional, and procedural paradigms.\n• **Primary Use Cases**: Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning (PyTorch, TensorFlow, Scikit-Learn), Web Development (Django, FastAPI, Flask), Data Analysis (Pandas, NumPy), and Automation/Scripting.\n• **Ecosystem**: Backed by a vast package repository (PyPI) and an active global developer community.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(49,23,'USER','How does cloud computing work?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(50,23,'AI','**Cloud Computing** is the on-demand delivery of computing services—including servers, storage, databases, networking, software, and analytics—over the internet (\'the cloud\') with pay-as-you-go pricing.\n\n• **How It Works**: Cloud providers (like AWS, Google Cloud, Azure) maintain massive distributed data centers. Users provision virtualized resources instantly via APIs or dashboards without buying physical hardware.\n• **Core Service Models**:\n  1. **IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service)**: Rent virtual machines and raw storage (e.g. AWS EC2, Google Compute Engine).\n  2. **PaaS (Platform as a Service)**: Deploy applications without managing underlying operating systems (e.g. Heroku, AWS Elastic Beanstalk).\n  3. **SaaS (Software as a Service)**: Complete cloud-hosted applications accessed via web browsers (e.g. Google Workspace, Microsoft 365).',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(51,24,'USER','Write a short paragraph about technology.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(52,24,'AI','Technology is the cornerstone of modern civilization, reshaping how humanity communicates, works, and solves complex global challenges. From intelligent software algorithms and ubiquitous mobile connectivity to cloud infrastructure and automated workflows, technological advancements accelerate human productivity and democratize access to knowledge worldwide. As digital systems continue to evolve, responsible innovation that prioritizes user privacy, data security, and sustainable computing remains vital to building an equitable and empowered future.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(53,25,'USER','Explain programming concepts.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(54,25,'AI','**Core Programming Concepts** form the foundational logic for developing robust software applications:\n\n1. **Variables & Data Types**: Containers for storing data (integers, floats, strings, booleans, collections).\n2. **Control Flow**: Directing program execution using conditionals (`if/else`) and loops (`for/while`).\n3. **Functions & Modularity**: Reusable blocks of code that take inputs, perform operations, and return outputs, reducing code duplication.\n4. **Data Structures**: Organized formats for storing data efficiently (Arrays, Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues, Hash Maps, Trees).\n5. **Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)**: Organizing code into objects and classes using Encapsulation, Inheritance, Polymorphism, and Abstraction.\n6. **Algorithms & Complexity**: Step-by-step procedures for solving problems, measured in Time and Space complexity (Big-O notation).',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:27:48'),(55,26,'USER','How many total files are stored in my IntelliFile?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(56,26,'AI','You currently have a total of **18 files** stored in your IntelliFile workspace.\n\n**Format Breakdown**: 12 PDF, 1 CSV, 1 XLSX, 1 DOCX, 1 PPTX, 1 JSON, 1 TXT.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(57,27,'USER','How many PDF, DOCX and PPT files do I have?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(58,27,'AI','Here is the breakdown of your files by format:\n• **PDF**: 12 files\n• **DOCX**: 1 file\n• **PPT**: 1 file\n\nMost used format: **PDF** (12 files).',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(59,28,'USER','How many important files are saved?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(60,28,'AI','You have **15 Important files** saved in your workspace.\n\n• **Important**: 15\n• **Normal**: 3\n• **Low**: 0\n\nTotal files: 18.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(61,29,'USER','How many files were uploaded today?',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(62,29,'AI','You currently have a total of **18 files** stored in your IntelliFile workspace.\n\n**Format Breakdown**: 12 PDF, 1 CSV, 1 XLSX, 1 DOCX, 1 PPTX, 1 JSON, 1 TXT.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(63,30,'USER','Show my recently uploaded files.',NULL,'2026-11-02 04:28:04'),(64,30,'AI','Here are your **5 most recently uploaded files** in IntelliFile:','[{\"id\":19,\"title\":\"AML Assignment.pdf\",\"format\":\"PDF\",\"size\":\"2.4 MB\",\"dateText\":\"Oct 30, 2026\",\"priority\":\"IMPORTANT\",\"category\":\"Assignment\",\"file_url\":null},{\"id