 identified in this document.\"]','[\"No specialized technical terms or definitions detected in this document.\"]','In conclusion, VitalSync_Health_Report_1793433669266.pdf provides a complete PDF reference record structured across 1 core informational areas.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(46,26,'FactScanAI_Project_Document.docx','DOCX','20.7 KB','uploads/documents/22a73c671a9873170802bcd5_FactScanAI_Project_Document.docx','Notes','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,1,'FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users check whether news, messages, and viral posts are trustworthy within seconds. Users can paste text, share a link, or upload a screenshot or image directly from messaging and social media apps. The AI analyzes the language, source, claims, and media, cross-checks them with trusted fact-checking sources, and returns a clear credibility verdict (Likely Real, Suspicious, or Likely Fake) with a confidence score and a simple explanation. Special focus is given to everyday users, students, and elderly or less tech-savvy people who receive large numbers of forwarded messages.\nMARKET RELEVANCE: Misinformation spreads faster than it can be corrected, especially through messaging apps and social media. False news about health, elections, finance, and public safety can cause panic, financial loss, and social harm. Professional fact-checking is accurate but slow and cannot cover every viral message. AI-driven verification tools offer instant, scalable, and accessible support, making this application highly relevant in today’s digital information environment.\nPROBLEM IT AIMS TO SOLVE:\nRapid spread of misinformation: Fake news and forwarded messages reach thousands of people within minutes, long before corrections appear.\nNo instant way to verify content: Professional fact-check articles take hours or days to publish, and ordinary users do not know where to check quickly.\nLow media and digital literacy: Many users, especially elderly and first-time internet users, cannot easily tell the difference between genuine and false content.\nUnverified forwards on messaging platforms: Content shared through private chats and groups spreads without source details or any verification.\nLanguage and accessibility barriers: Most fact-checking resources are limited to a few languages, leaving many regional language users without support.\nManipulated images and misleading media: Edited photos, old images reused in new contexts, and AI-generated media are hard to identify with the naked eye.\nINTRODUCTION:\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: Fake news has become a serious social and economic problem. Traditional fact-checking depends on human experts and cannot match the speed and volume of online content. Without a quick and understandable way to verify information, users unknowingly believe and share false content, which increases its reach and harm.\nPURPOSE: The purpose of this application is to provide an AI-powered fake news detection assistant that gives instant, explainable credibility checks, helps users make informed sharing decisions, and builds long-term awareness against misinformation.\nSCOPE: The application focuses on text, link, and image-based news verification, credibility scoring, source and evidence checking, and user awareness reporting. It is designed for general social media and messaging users, students, elderly users, and communities with limited access to fact-checking resources.\nGPCU\nG – Gap Analysis\nNo instant verification of viral content: Fact-checking articles are slow, and users cannot get a quick answer at the moment they receive a suspicious message.\nFact-checks not available where content is shared: Verification tools are separate from messaging and social apps, so users rarely take extra steps to check.\nLimited regional language coverage: Existing resources mostly support a few major languages, excluding many users who consume news in regional languages.\nLack of clear explanations: Many tools only label content as true or false without showing the reasons, which reduces user trust and learning.\nText and image checks handled separately: Users must use different tools to verify claims and images, with no single combined analysis.\nP – Product (App)\nInstant multi-input news checking: Users can paste text, enter a link, upload a screenshot, or share content directly from other apps for analysis.\nAI-based credibility analysis and scoring: NLP models analyze writing style, emotional manipulation, clickbait patterns, and claims to generate a credibility score.\nCross-verification with trusted sources: The system compares claims with fact-checking databases and reputed news sources and evaluates the reliability of the original source.\nImage and media verification: Reverse image search and manipulation analysis detect edited, reused, or misleading images.\nExplainable results and history: Each result includes a clear explanation and evidence links, and past checks are saved with shareable fact-check cards.\nC – Competition Analysis:\nCompetitor\nType\nLocation\nProduct Offering\nPrice\nBusiness Size\nTarget Audience\nUnique Value Proposition\nProfessional Fact-Checking Websites\nDirect\nGlobal\nArticles that verify viral claims, written by trained journalists and editors\nFree\nMedium\nReaders, journalists and students\nExpert-verified, trusted and detailed analysis\nSocial Media Flagging & Community Notes\nIndirect\nGlobal\nPlatform warning labels, user reports and crowd-sourced context on posts\nFree\nLarge\nSocial media users\nBuilt into the platform where content is seen\nManual Self-Verification (Search / Reverse Image)\nIndirect\nLocal\nUsers search the web, compare sources or run reverse image search themselves\nFree\nSmall\nIndividuals checking news on their own\nSimple, no extra tools needed\nAI Detection Tools & Browser Extensions\nDirect\nGlobal\nAutomated credibility checks for articles and websites\nFree to Medium\nSmall to Medium\nTech-savvy users and researchers\nAutomated, quick analysis of web content\nU – Uniqueness:\nResults in seconds: Provides instant credibility checks instead of waiting hours or days for manual fact-check articles.\nExplainable verdicts with evidence: Shows why content is flagged, along with confidence levels and source links, so users can verify for themselves.\nEasy sharing from any app: Share-sheet integration lets users send content from messaging and social apps directly to FactScan AI.\nMultilingual and simple design: Designed with a simple interface and regional language support for users with basic technical knowledge.\nTrending misinformation alerts: Warns users about viral false claims in circulation so they can avoid sharing them.\nFUTURE SCOPE\nMultilingual and regional language support: The system will analyze and explain news in many regional languages to reach diverse users.\nDeepfake video and audio detection: AI will identify manipulated or synthetic videos and voice recordings.\nMessaging chatbot and browser extension: Users will be able to verify content directly inside messaging apps and web browsers.\nCommunity reporting and trend detection: User reports will help identify fast-spreading misinformation and trigger early warnings.\nVoice input and audio explanations: Users will check news by speaking and receive spoken results, improving accessibility.\nGamified media literacy modules: Quizzes, challenges, and badges will teach users how to recognize fake news and increase engagement.\nWHY USERS WILL USE THIS APP EVEN AFTER TESTING IS DONE\nQuick verification on the go – Enables users to check any message or post in seconds without searching multiple websites.\nTrusted and understandable results – Provides clear verdicts with explanations and sources that users can rely on.\nProtecting family and friends – Shareable fact-check cards help users correct misinformation and stop false forwards.\nPersonalized alerts – Notifies users about trending false claims related to their language and topics of interest.\nMotivational awareness tracking – Displays awareness streaks, badges, and verification history to encourage responsible sharing habits.\nDESIGN AND ENGINEERING STANDARDS\nUser-Centered Design\nSimple interface for all users: The application uses a clean one-screen layout with clear color-coded verdicts for users with basic technical knowledge.\nVoice-guided navigation: Audio instructions and spoken results assist users in checking news and understanding outcomes.\nAccessibility-friendly design: The system supports readable fonts, clear buttons, high contrast, and inclusive design for elderly and differently-abled users.\nSeparate user and moderator dashboards: Dedicated dashboards provide verification features for users and review and monitoring tools for moderators and fact-checkers.\nSoftware Engineering Practices\nFlutter / Android with MVVM architecture: The app follows structured MVVM design for better maintainability and performance.\nPython backend services: Python (FastAPI) handles authentication, database, NLP and image analysis services, and notifications for reliable backend support.\nSecure RESTful API communication: All data exchange is protected using secure HTTPS-based API communication.\nModular and scalable application design: The system is built in modules (text analysis, source checking, image forensics, evidence retrieval), allowing easy upgrades and future feature expansion.\nDATA SECURITY & PRIVACY\nSecure data encryption – User credentials and submitted content are protected using AES-256 encryption for storage and TLS encryption during data transmission.\nSecure authentication system – Authentication is handled through Firebase Authentication with JWT-based session management to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nPrivacy and data compliance – The system follows GDPR-based data protection principles, including user consent, secure data handling, and activity logging.\nRole-based access control (RBAC) – Only authorized moderators and administrators can access review queues and system data, ensuring restricted and secure information sharing.\nProtected submission storage – Submitted messages and images are stored securely with limited retention, anonymized logging, and strict privacy controls to safeguard user confidentiality.\nPERFORMANCE STANDARDS\nLow-latency AI processing – Lightweight models, optimized API calls, and caching of previously verified claims ensure results within seconds.\nOffline history caching – Caching techniques allow users to access past checks and saved results even without continuous internet connectivity.\nTimely push notifications – Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) delivers alerts about trending misinformation and completed checks.\nOptimized media handling – Compressed image processing maintains analysis quality while improving performance and reducing data usage.\nEfficient battery management – The application is optimized to minimize battery consumption during image analysis and background operations.\nTESTING AND QUALITY ASSURANCE\nComprehensive functional testing – Unit testing, integration testing, and UI testing ensure stability across core features such as login, news submission, and verdict display.\nAutomated CI/CD testing pipeline – Continuous integration and deployment pipelines automatically test and validate system updates for reliability and performance.\nCross-device compatibility testing – The application is tested across multiple Android and iOS devices to ensure smooth performance on different screen sizes and OS versions.\nScalability and load testing – Load testing validates system performance when many users submit content at the same time, such as during viral news events.\nDetection accuracy and bias testing – Precision, recall, and F1-score are measured on labeled datasets, and results are checked across topics and languages to reduce bias.\nINTEROPERABILITY STANDARDS\nReport and fact-check card export – Users can download or share verification results as images or PDF reports for easy sharing and record keeping.\nFact-check database and API integration – The system connects with public fact-checking databases and APIs, such as the Google Fact Check Tools API, to retrieve existing verified claims.\nShare-sheet integration – The application accepts text, links, and images shared directly from other apps on the device.\nETHICAL & TRANSPARENCY STANDARDS\nTransparent AI operation – Users are clearly informed that results are AI-based probabilities, not absolute truth, and are shown confidence levels, reasons, and source links.\nUser consent and data permission – In-app consent forms ensure users provide explicit approval before submitted content is analyzed or stored.\nStrict data privacy protection – User data is never shared with third parties without clear permission, ensuring confidentiality and secure usage.\nNeutral and bias-aware verification – The system is designed to be non-partisan, evidence-based, and regularly tested so that it does not favor any political, religious, or social group.\nSupportive feedback design – Results and alerts are worded respectfully to educate users without blaming or shaming them, and users can report incorrect results for human review.\nRELEVANT STANDARDS\nSafety Standards\nISO/IEC 27001 – Information Security Management – Provides guidelines for protecting sensitive user information such as submitted messages, images, and personal details. It ensures secure storage, encryption, and controlled access within the application.\nISO/IEC 23053 – AI System Framework – Supports the design and governance of machine-learning-based systems. It ensures that the detection algorithms operate reliably, transparently, and safely when evaluating content.\nISO/IEC 42001 – AI Management System – Provides requirements for responsible management of AI systems, covering risk assessment, accountability, and continuous improvement of the detection models.\nISO/IEC TR 24027 – Bias in AI Systems – Gives guidance on identifying and reducing bias in AI-assisted decision making, supporting fair verdicts across topics, languages, and communities.\nData Privacy & Security Standards\nGDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) – Ensures that user submissions and personal information are collected, stored, and processed with proper user consent and transparency.\nISO/IEC 27701 – Privacy Information Management – Extends ISO 27001 by adding privacy controls for managing sensitive submitted content and personal information within the system.\nDPDP Act 2023 (India) – Digital Personal Data Protection – Sets rules for lawful processing, consent, and protection of personal data of users in India, guiding how the application handles submitted content.\nSoftware & Mobile Application Quality Standards\nISO/IEC 25010 – Software Quality Model – Defines quality attributes such as reliability, usability, performance efficiency, security, and maintainability. This ensures the application provides a stable and effective verification platform.\nISO/IEC 29119 – Software Testing Standard – Provides structured guidelines for software testing processes including unit, integration, and system testing to ensure accurate analysis and reliable application performance.\nIEEE 7000 – Ethical Considerations in System Design – Guides the responsible development of AI-driven systems. It ensures fairness, transparency, and ethical behavior when the AI evaluates content and presents verdicts.\nUsability & Accessibility Standards\nISO 9241-210 – Human-Centered Design for Interactive Systems – Ensures the application is designed based on user needs, especially for elderly and first-time digital users, improving usability and accessibility.\nWCAG 2.1 – Web Content Accessibility Guidelines – Ensures accessible design features such as readable text, clear navigation, and compatibility with assistive technologies.\nISO 9241-11 – Usability Standard – Provides guidelines to ensure the application is easy to use, efficient, and effective for users verifying news content.\n2D Design\n[Insert your hand-drawn 2D wireframe here]\nSuggested layout (four panels):\nUSER PROFILE — Name, Age, Phone No, Email, Preferred Language\nAI ANALYSIS — Credibility analysis graph, Credibility Score (e.g., 84%), Confidence\nCHECK NEWS — Paste Text [Start], Paste Link [Start], Upload Screenshot [Start]\nVERDICT & SUGGESTIONS — Likely Real / Suspicious / Likely Fake, Evidence Report, Logout\n3D Design\n[Insert your 3D mockup image here]\nSuggested screens: User Profile • AI Credibility Analysis • Check News (Text / Link / Image) • Verdict, Evidence & Suggestions\nFUNCTIONAL PROTOTYPE\nIdea Scanning & System Architecture Analysis\nUser onboarding and preference setup – Users register in the application and provide basic details such as preferred language, topics of interest, and notification preferences.\nAI-based content analysis pipeline – The AI backend processes submitted text, links, or images through text analysis, source checking, evidence retrieval, and image verification, and generates a credibility verdict with an explanation.\nUser Authentication and Profiles\nSecure authentication system – Provides secure signup, login, and logout with encrypted sessions to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nUser profile management – Allows users to manage personal details such as age, language, topics of interest, and alert settings.\nImage and profile upload – Users can upload profile photos and screenshots or images of news for verification.\nAI-BASED FAKE NEWS DETECTION MODULE\nNews submission through mobile interface – Users paste text, enter a link, upload a screenshot, or share content from other apps for checking.\nAI credibility analysis – The AI evaluates writing style, emotional language, clickbait patterns, source reputation, and claim matches with known fact-checks.\nVerdict with confidence and explanation – Each result is labeled Likely Real, Suspicious, or Likely Fake with a confidence score, reasons, and evidence links.\nReal-time guidance – The system provides instant suggestions such as “Do not forward,” “Check the official website,” or “Verify with a trusted source.”\nPERSONALIZED ALERTS & LEARNING\nAdaptive AI improvement – The AI improves its accuracy over time using moderator reviews and user feedback on results.\nCustomized alert preferences – Each user receives trending misinformation alerts based on their language, region, and topics of interest.\nPROGRESS MONITORING & REPORTS\nVisual history tracking – Daily and weekly charts display the number of checks and the share of real, suspicious, and fake results.\nPerformance indicators – Credibility scores and confidence levels are shown in a simple and understandable format.\nAwareness tracking – Visible progress charts encourage users to verify content before sharing.\nReport sharing capability – Fact-check cards and reports can be exported and shared with family, friends, or groups.\nREMINDERS & MOTIVATION SYSTEM\nTrending misinformation alerts – Notifications warn users about viral false claims currently circulating.\nVerification streak tracking – Tracks consecutive days of checking content before sharing to encourage responsible habits.\nAchievement badges and rewards – Rewards such as “10 Verified Checks” motivate users to stay engaged and keep verifying.\nUTILITY & SETTINGS\nUser account controls – Includes Change Password, Edit Profile, Notifications, Logout, and Delete Account for full account management.\nSecure data handling – Ensures strong privacy protection, secure storage, and safe access to user submissions and history.\nTESTING AND VALIDATION OF PROTOTYPE\nStructured system workflow validation – The application follows a clear flow: Splash Screen → User Login → News Submission (Text/Link/Image) → AI Analysis → Verdict & Evidence → Moderator Dashboard.\nReal-time AI analysis testing – Credibility analysis and verdict generation are validated through a secure API connection with the AI engine.\nUsability and accuracy validation – Testing confirms reliable content analysis, accurate verdicts, and an easy-to-use interface suitable for all users.\nSystem reliability verification – Testing verifies system stability, alert delivery, and the effectiveness of explainable verdicts.\nIMPACT OF PROTOTYPE\nBridging manual and automated fact-checking – The AI-based system connects professional fact-checking with instant digital verification, giving users quick and trustworthy guidance at the moment they need it.\nEmpowering informed sharing – The system enables users to check content independently and make responsible decisions before forwarding, while allowing human moderators to review difficult cases.\nImproving awareness and community safety – The prototype slows the spread of false information, improves media literacy, and reduces the harm caused by misinformation through intelligent automation.\nCONCLUSION\nFactScan AI — Instant Fake News Detection is more than a basic news checking application — it functions as a smart digital fact-checking assistant. By providing real-time AI-based analysis, explainable verdicts, and continuous awareness tracking, the system improves information accuracy, user confidence, and responsible sharing habits. With its scalable AI-driven architecture and user-centered design, the platform has strong potential to expand into multilingual verification, deepfake detection, community-based reporting, and broader digital literacy solutions, helping build a more trustworthy information environment through advanced mobile technology.','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-05 05:00:32','READY','FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users check whether news, messages, and viral posts are trustworthy within seconds. INTRODUCTION:\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: Fake news has become a serious social and economic problem. PURPOSE: The purpose of this application is to provide an AI-powered fake news detection assistant that gives instant, explainable credibility checks, helps users make informed sharing decisions, and builds long-term awareness against misinformation.','[\"Users\",\"User\",\"Standards\",\"Fake\",\"News\"]','[\"Explainable results and history: Each result includes a clear explanation and evidence links, and past checks are saved with shareable fact-check cards.\",\"PERFORMANCE STANDARDS\\nLow-latency AI processing – Lightweight models, optimized API calls, and caching of previously verified claims ensure results within seconds.\",\"RELEVANT STANDARDS\\nSafety Standards\\nISO\\/IEC 27001 – Information Security Management – Provides guidelines for protecting sensitive user information such as submitted messages, images, and personal details.\",\"ISO\\/IEC 42001 – AI Management System – Provides requirements for responsible management of AI systems, covering risk assessment, accountability, and continuous improvement of the detection models.\",\"Software & Mobile Application Quality Standards\\nISO\\/IEC 25010 – Software Quality Model – Defines quality attributes such as reliability, usability, performance efficiency, security, and maintainability.\",\"ISO\\/IEC 29119 – Software Testing Standard – Provides structured guidelines for software testing processes including unit, integration, and system testing to ensure accurate analysis and reliable application performance.\",\"ISO 9241-11 – Usability Standard – Provides guidelines to ensure the application is easy to use, efficient, and effective for users verifying news content.\",\"Real-time guidance – The system provides instant suggestions such as “Do not forward,” “Check the official website,” or “Verify with a trusted source.”\\nPERSONALIZED ALERTS & LEARNING\\nAdaptive AI improvement – The AI improves its accuracy over time using moderator reviews and user feedback on results.\"]','[\"FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users check whether news, messages, and viral posts are trustworthy within seconds.\",\"Users can paste text, share a link, or upload a screenshot or image directly from messaging and social media apps.\",\"Special focus is given to everyday users, students, and elderly or less tech-savvy people who receive large numbers of forwarded messages.\",\"No instant way to verify content: Professional fact-check articles take hours or days to publish, and ordinary users do not know where to check quickly.\",\"Low media and digital literacy: Many users, especially elderly and first-time internet users, cannot easily tell the difference between genuine and false content.\",\"Language and accessibility barriers: Most fact-checking resources are limited to a few languages, leaving many regional language users without support.\",\"Without a quick and understandable way to verify information, users unknowingly believe and share false content, which increases its reach and harm.\"]','[\"FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users check whether news, messages, and viral posts are trustworthy within seconds.\",\"Users can paste text, share a link, or upload a screenshot or image directly from messaging and social media apps.\",\"Special focus is given to everyday users, students, and elderly or less tech-savvy people who receive large numbers of forwarded messages.\",\"No instant way to verify content: Professional fact-check articles take hours or days to publish, and ordinary users do not know where to check quickly.\",\"Low media and digital literacy: Many users, especially elderly and first-time internet users, cannot easily tell the difference between genuine and false content.\",\"Language and accessibility barriers: Most fact-checking resources are limited to a few languages, leaving many regional language users without support.\",\"Without a quick and understandable way to verify information, users unknowingly believe and share false content, which increases its reach and harm.\"]','[\"AI — FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users\",\"FAKE — FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users\",\"NEWS — FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users\",\"APP — FACTSCAN AI — INSTANT FAKE NEWS DETECTION\\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\\nAPP OVERVIEW: FactScan AI is an intelligent mobile application that helps users\",\"MARKET — MARKET RELEVANCE: Misinformation spreads faster than it can be corrected, especially through messaging apps and social media.\",\"IT — PROBLEM IT AIMS TO SOLVE:\\nRapid spread of misinformation: Fake news and forwarded messages reach thousands of people within minutes, long be\"]','CONCLUSION\nFactScan AI — Instant Fake News Detection is more than a basic news checking application — it functions as a smart digital fact-checking assistant.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(50,18,'IntelliFile_AI_Presentation  og.pptx','PPTX','4.8 MB','uploads/documents/ffc40526e9a832a512b1dafa_IntelliFile_AI_Presentationog.pptx','Document','Internal Storage','IMPORTANT',0,0,25,'Slide 1: INTELLIFILE AI Find. Prioritize. Access. IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R. KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\n\nSlide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date. Finding the right file on time is slow, and important files get buried. Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists. No Prioritization: Urgent and low-value files look the same. Scattered Files: Downloads, WhatsApp and browser files end up in different places. Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents. Solution AI Smart Search: Find files with natural-language questions. AI Prioritization: Mark documents Important, Normal or Low. AI Vault: Index selected documents for AI analysis and insights. Privacy by Design: Only documents are accessed, and only with consent.\n\nSlide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails. Important documents (IDs, policies, assignments) get lost among 100+ other files. Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data. IntelliFile finds files using natural language, e.g. “find Kishore ppt”. Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters. The AI Vault indexes chosen documents and shows AI Insights. Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\n\nSlide 4: Product domain study SUMMARY: IntelliFile AI is an AI-powered document management app for Android. It scans documents on the device (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV and more), shows them in one organised place, and lets users search with plain language. Each document can be marked Important, Normal or Low, saved for quick access, or moved to the AI Vault where it is indexed for AI analysis. Unlike ordinary file managers, IntelliFile focuses on finding the right document quickly and on keeping urgent files visible, while only accessing documents and never photos or media without consent. ARTICLE: Digital documents pile up fast on a student’s or professional’s phone. IntelliFile AI turns that pile into an organised , searchable library. Its AI assistant answers requests like “find my Kishore files” across Device Files and the AI Vault, while a priority dashboard shows how many documents are Important, Normal or Low. CONCLUSION: IntelliFile AI brings search, prioritization and privacy together in one simple app. By helping users find, prioritize and access files easily, it saves time and reduces the stress of lost or forgotten documents\n\nSlide 5: Problem Statement Existing file managers list documents only by name and date, so finding the right file in 100+ documents takes too long. Users cannot easily tell which documents are urgent, which are routine, and which can be ignored. Documents downloaded from browsers and WhatsApp are scattered, and users are not alerted when new files arrive. Many apps ask for broad access to photos and media, which raises privacy concerns. There is a clear need for a lightweight, AI-powered Android app that finds, prioritizes and opens documents quickly and respects privacy.\n\nSlide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE MY RESPONSIBILITIES The goal is to design and build a mobile app that helps users find, prioritize and access their documents easily. It works through AI natural-language search, priority tagging, an AI Vault for indexed documents, and simple, secure file permissions. Designing the app interface and navigation. Building file listing, search and priority modules. Developing the AI chat and AI Vault features. Adding notifications, themes and profile settings. Testing the app with users for smooth performance. Collecting feedback and improving the design.\n\nSlide 7: Project Plan\n\nSlide 8: USER 1 TA Name: Tamil azahagan Age: 21 Occupation: MCA Student Location: Chennai GOAL : Tamil azahagan wants to open the right assignment or presentation within seconds, and to keep urgent files at the top. FRUSTRATION : His phone holds 150+ PDFs, slides and notes from many classes. Before a viva she spends 10+ minutes scrolling for one document. Important files look the same as old, unused ones. PROBLEM STATEMENT : Students need a way to search documents quickly and see which files matter most. IntelliFile helps through natural-language search, priority tags (Important / Normal / Low) and a Saved list for quick access.\n\nSlide 9: USER 2 VI Name: vinnoli Age: 26 Occupation: Software Engineer Location: Chennai GOAL : vinnoli wants to find any work document by describing it, and to be notified when new files are downloaded, without giving up privacy. FRUSTRATION : Documents arrive from email, browser and WhatsApp into different folders. He often misses deadlines because urgent files are hidden. He avoids apps that need access to his photos and media. PROBLEM STATEMENT : Working professionals need one place to see all documents, spot urgent ones and get alerts about new downloads. IntelliFile offers document-only access, new-document alerts, quiet hours and an AI Vault with insights.\n\nSlide 10: User Journey Map Persona : Tamilazahagan , 21, Student   |   Goal: To quickly find, prioritize and open documents on her phone. ACTION TASK LIST FEELING ADJECTIVE IMPROVEMENT OPPORTUNITIES Grant Access a. Open the app and allow document storage access. b. Read the privacy note. I feel safe and in control. Add a short onboarding walkthrough. Browse Files a. Open Files and view Device Files. b. Filter by PDF, DOC, PPT or Other. I feel organised. Faster loading for large libraries. Prioritize a. Mark files Important, Normal or Low. b. Check the priority dashboard. I feel in charge. Suggest priorities automatically. Ask the AI a. Type or speak a file name. b. Open the result. I feel impressed and saved time. Improve answers for vague queries. Use the AI Vault a. Move key documents into the vault. b. View AI Insights. I feel confident and informed. Richer summaries and deadline alerts.\n\nSlide 11: Competitive analysis Competitor Strengths Limitations IntelliFile’s Differentiator Files by Google Clean interface, fast cleanup tools and file sharing. No priority levels; search is mostly by file name. AI search plus Important / Normal / Low prioritization. Typical File Managers (ES, Solid) Powerful folder control and many file operations. Cluttered; no AI help or document ranking. Simple, document-focused layout with AI assistant. Google Drive Cloud storage with strong search. Needs uploads and internet; privacy concerns for local files. Works on local device files with document-only access. Cloud Note / Doc Apps Good for documents created inside the app. Do not manage files already on the device. Finds and prioritizes existing device and WhatsApp files.\n\nSlide 12: Business Potential IntelliFile AI targets anyone who handles many digital documents. Students (40%) and working professionals (30%) form the largest group, followed by small business owners (20%) and researchers or others (10%). These users need fast, reliable file access every day, which gives the app strong adoption potential. With AI search, priority tagging and a privacy-first approach, it can stand out from ordinary file managers. (Audience split shown is an estimate for presentation.)\n\nSlide 13: User Pain Points Time Wasted Searching: Scrolling through long file lists just to find one document wastes time, especially before exams, meetings and deadlines. No Sense of Priority: Urgent and unimportant files are mixed together, so users cannot tell what to open first and may miss deadlines. Scattered Downloads: Files from browsers and WhatsApp land in different folders, and users are not told when something new arrives. Privacy Worries: Many apps request access to photos and media. Users want an app that touches documents only.\n\nSlide 14: Flow Diagram Login / Sign Up Home Grant Document Access Files Device Files AI Vault Priority Dashboard AI Ask / Voice Search Open Result Chat History Saved Saved Files Priority Filter Open / Share Profile Edit Profile Theme · Notifications Help & Support\n\nSlide 15: App Screens: Files Priority Dashboard AI Document Vault Recent Files: Other Recent Files: PPT\n\nSlide 16: App Screens: AI & Saved IntelliFile AI Home AI File Search Results AI Chat History Saved Files by Priority\n\nSlide 17: App Screens: Profile & Settings Edit Profile Profile Picture Options Notifications Theme\n\nSlide 18: App Screens: Permissions & Support File Permissions About IntelliFile Help & Support Contact Support\n\nSlide 19: Usability Studies Round 1: Initial Study Participants: 5–7 users (students and working professionals) Search Issues: Some queries returned no match when file names were spelled differently. Low Clarity: Priority labels were not obvious at first. Navigation: Users wanted faster access to Saved files. Improvement: Add bottom tab bar and filter chips. Round 2: Refined Study Participants: 5–7 new users Improved Navigation: The bottom bar made switching tabs quick. Clear Priorities: Colour-coded tags helped users spot urgent files. Trust: The privacy note on File Permissions increased confidence. Final Recommendation: Add onboarding and smarter suggestions.\n\nSlide 20: List of Components Component Technology Specifications Mobile Application Android app Material-style interface with bottom navigation: Home, AI, Files, Saved, Profile. File Scanner Device storage access Reads documents only (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV, TXT) from Internal Storage and Downloads. AI Search Assistant Natural-language search + voice Finds files across Device Files and the AI Vault and keeps chat history. AI Document Vault Indexing and AI analysis Stores selected documents as indexed items and offers AI Insights. Priority Engine Tags and filters Marks files Important, Normal or Low; shows dashboard counts and saved list. Notification System Alerts + quiet hours Notifies on new downloads and silences alerts from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM.\n\nSlide 21: Project learning Project Impact What I Learnt IntelliFile AI makes it faster and less stressful to manage documents on a phone. AI search, priority tags and an AI Vault turn a long list of files into a clear, usable library, while the document-only permission model keeps personal data private. It can help students and professionals save time and avoid missing important files. Technological Innovation: Integrating AI search, file indexing and mobile UI into one app. Problem-Solving Skills: Handling permissions, large file lists, and priority logic. Impact of Technology: Seeing how AI and privacy-first design can improve everyday productivity.\n\nSlide 22: Product Design Patent PATENT Claim 1: A document management system that assigns Important, Normal or Low priority to files and displays priority counts in a dashboard and a filtered Saved list. Claim 2: An AI assistant that accepts typed or spoken natural-language queries and returns matching files from both device storage and an AI Vault. Claim 3: A privacy-first access model that reads only documents, indexes user-selected files into an AI Vault, and sends new-document alerts with automatic quiet hours.\n\nSlide 23: Next Steps Step A: Design Refinement Refine UI using usability feedback. Improve AI search for vague queries. Add onboarding walkthrough and more languages. Step B: Prototyping and Testing Build a high-fidelity prototype with full AI integration. Test on different Android devices. Run beta testing with real users. Step C: Documentation and Filing Prepare technical documentation for patent filing. Create user manual and onboarding guide. Finalise privacy policy and terms of service.\n\nSlide 24: Step D: Compliance and Approvals Google Play Approvals Follow Google Play policies for storage and file access permissions. Use Material Design guidelines for consistent UI/UX. Test on multiple Android versions and screen sizes. Publish clear privacy policy and terms before submission. Prepare app name, screenshots, description and category. Privacy, Quality and Security Data Privacy: Handle documents securely and follow applicable privacy laws. Access Control: Keep to document-only access with explicit consent. Security Testing: Third-party testing of AI Vault and storage handling. Reliability: Regular updates to meet store policies.\n\nSlide 25: THANK YOU E-mail: kishoreraja437@gmail.com Name:R . Kishore Reg No: 252524002','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 04:45:05','READY','IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R. AI Vault: Index selected documents for AI analysis and insights. Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.','[\"Project Plan\",\"Slide\",\"Files\",\"Vault\",\"Intellifile\"]','[\"Finding the right file on time is slow, and important files get buried.\",\"AI Prioritization: Mark documents Important, Normal or Low.\",\"Important documents (IDs, policies, assignments) get lost among 100+ other files.\",\"Slide 5: Problem Statement Existing file managers list documents only by name and date, so finding the right file in 100+ documents takes too long.\",\"Slide 16: App Screens: AI & Saved IntelliFile AI Home AI File Search Results AI Chat History Saved Files by Priority\",\"Notification System Alerts + quiet hours Notifies on new downloads and silences alerts from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM.\",\"Slide 22: Product Design Patent PATENT Claim 1: A document management system that assigns Important, Normal or Low priority to files and displays priority counts in a dashboard and a filtered Saved list.\",\"Claim 3: A privacy-first access model that reads only documents, indexes user-selected files into an AI Vault, and sends new-document alerts with automatic quiet hours.\"]','[\"Slide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date.\",\"Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists.\",\"Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents.\",\"Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.\",\"Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data.\",\"Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters.\",\"Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\"]','[\"Slide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date.\",\"Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists.\",\"Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents.\",\"Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.\",\"Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data.\",\"Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters.\",\"Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\"]','[\"AI — Slide 1: INTELLIFILE AI Find.\",\"BY — IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R.\",\"BSC — KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\",\"AIDS — KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\",\"XLSX — It scans documents on the device (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV and more), shows them in one organised place, and lets users search with plain la\",\"MY — Slide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE MY RESPONSIBILITIES The goal is to design and build a mobile app that helps users find, prioritize and access\"]','Kishore Reg No: 252524002',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(51,18,'StockSense Product Review.pptx','PPTX','1.8 MB','uploads/documents/97ee2b6fa01be4c7a3a887bc_StockSenseProductReview.pptx','Document','Internal Storage','NORMAL',0,0,32,'Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP StockSense Smarter stock. Better business. AI-assisted inventory intelligence for medium-sized supermarkets. BY · NAME: [Your name] · REG NO: [Reg no] · DEP: [Department]\n\nSlide 2: THE PROBLEM Product problem Medium-sized supermarkets run on guesswork, not data. That leads to: Stock-outs Popular items run out, and the sale is lost. Dead stock Cash is locked in items that no longer sell. Guessed reorders Orders depend on memory and gut feel. No next step Billing tools store numbers but rarely say what to do. 2\n\nSlide 3: OVERVIEW Project overview THE PROBLEM Reorders are guessed, so popular items run out. Slow and dead stock locks up cash. Billing software records data but gives little guidance. Owners have little time to read reports. THE SOLUTION Import stock from CSV or Excel, with checks and column mapping. A dashboard of sales, low stock, slow-moving and dead stock. Recommendations that show the numbers behind them. Dukaan Mitra, an assistant that answers shop questions in English, Hindi and Tamil. 3\n\nSlide 4: DOMAIN STUDY Product domain study SUMMARY StockSense is an Android app for retail inventory management. It turns a supermarket\'s stock and sales data into clear actions: what to reorder, what to clear, and what sells together. KEY IDEAS IN THIS DOMAIN Stock cover: how many days current stock will last. Reorder point: when to order again, so the shelf never empties. Slow-moving vs dead stock: few sales versus none. Market basket: items customers buy together, which suits bundles. 4\n\nSlide 5: DOMAIN STUDY LinkedIn article Article  StockSense is an Android app that helps supermarket owners decide what to reorder, what to clear and what to bundle. Owners import stock from a CSV or Excel file, record sales, and see low stock, slow-moving and dead stock on one dashboard. Every recommendation shows the numbers behind it, so owners can check it. A built-in assistant, Dukaan Mitra, answers shop questions in English, Hindi and Tamil. CONCLUSION StockSense turns everyday sales data into practical, explainable decisions. LINKEDIN [Paste article link] 5\n\nSlide 6: PROBLEM STATEMENT What we set out to fix Medium-sized supermarkets lose sales to stock-outs and lock up cash in slow-moving stock. Existing tools record sales but rarely say what to do next, or why. Owners need a simple, mobile app that turns stock and sales data into clear, explainable actions. StockSense: a lightweight, explainable, mobile-first inventory intelligence app. 6\n\nSlide 7: SCOPE Project scope MY ROLE Design and build StockSense end to end: the Android app, the PHP and MySQL backend, and the AI assistant. The goal is an app that helps supermarket owners manage stock and act on clear recommendations. MY RESPONSIBILITIES Designing the app UI: Bold Outline style, light and dark themes. Building import, inventory, sales, reorder and insights modules. Integrating the Dukaan Mitra AI assistant. Testing on real phones and with automated test suites. Reviewing and refining AI-assisted code. 7\n\nSlide 8: PLAN · 27 SEP TO 10 DEC 2026 Project plan # Phase Dates 1 Topic selection [add dates] 2 GPCU [add dates] 3 Requirement gathering [add dates] 4 Design phase using Figma [add dates] 5 Frontend [add dates] 6 Backend [add dates] 7 Integration phase [add dates] 8 Testing stage [add dates] 9 Deployment [add dates] 8\n\nSlide 9: MILESTONES Project timeline 13 Oct StockSense chosen as the project 23 Oct All screens built, tested on a phone 29 Oct Backend done: auth, import, sales, reorder, insights 2 Nov App connected to the backend 4 Nov Push alerts live; AI assistant planned 16 Nov Icons, weekly digest and cleanup done 17 Nov Bold Outline redesign and dark mode 19 Nov Demo data, import fixes, review ready 9\n\nSlide 10: USER PERSONA 1 The shop owner O [Name], 45 Owner, medium supermarket Illustrative persona GOALS Never run out of fast sellers. Free cash from slow stock. PAIN POINTS Checks shelves by eye. Reorders by memory. Finds dead stock too late. WHAT STOCKSENSE GIVES One dashboard: low stock, slow stock and clear reorder advice. 10\n\nSlide 11: USER PERSONA 2 The store staff member S [Name], 24 Billing and shelf staff Illustrative persona GOALS Record sales fast. Update stock when new goods arrive. PAIN POINTS Typing stock by hand. Not sure what the owner wants restocked. WHAT STOCKSENSE GIVES Quick bill entry, file import for stock, and Dukaan Mitra to ask in simple words. 11\n\nSlide 12: USER JOURNEY From sign-up to action Stage What the user does What StockSense does Sign up Creates a shop account Keeps each shop\'s data separate Import Uploads a CSV or Excel file Matches columns, previews changes Sell Records bills Updates stock instantly Review Opens the dashboard Shows low, slow and dead stock Act Follows advice or asks Dukaan Mitra Explains with real numbers 12\n\nSlide 13: COMPETITOR ANALYSIS Where StockSense fits Product Strength Gap StockSense targets Vyapar Billing and inventory for small businesses Explainable reorder and slow-stock advice GoFrugal [verify] Full retail ERP Lighter, mobile-first, simple setup Marg ERP [verify] Broad accounting and stock Chat assistant in local languages Zoho Inventory [verify] Multi-channel inventory Built for single supermarkets 13\n\nSlide 14: MARKET POTENTIAL Why the need is real Stock-outs and stock-record inaccuracy in retail 91% Share of stock typically affected 28–40% Share of sales lost 9% 14\n\nSlide 15: VALUE What the owner sees 14 opportunities found 4 reorder, 5 slow or dead, 5 bundles ₹12,072 tied up in slow-moving stock Cash that could be freed Each opportunity shows the numbers behind it, so the owner can check before acting. 15\n\nSlide 16: PAIN POINTS Problems and our answers STOCK-OUTS Fast sellers run out unnoticed. Low-stock alerts and reorder advice. DEAD STOCK Cash sits on shelves for months. Slow and dead stock flagged with value. MANUAL ENTRY Typing hundreds of products is slow. CSV and Excel import with preview. BLACK-BOX TOOLS Advice without reasons is hard to trust. Every number comes from the shop\'s own data. 16\n\nSlide 17: DESIGN PROCESS Product sketches (1 of 2) Splash Login Sign up Home Inventory 17\n\nSlide 18: DESIGN PROCESS Product sketches (2 of 2) Product details Import stock Record sale Insights Dukaan Mitra 18\n\nSlide 19: DESIGN PHASE Figma designs Home Inventory Insights 19\n\nSlide 20: DESIGN PHASE Figma designs Product details Dukaan Mitra Alerts 20\n\nSlide 21: APP FLOW How the app works 1 Sign up 2 Add or import stock 3 Review preview 4 Record sales then 5 Dashboard updates 6 Insights and reorder 7 Alerts and weekly digest 8 Ask Dukaan Mitra 21\n\nSlide 22: FLOW DIAGRAM Screen-to-screen flow Login / Sign up → Home Bottom navigation Inventory Product details, edit, import Insights Reorder, slow stock, bundles Sales Add products to a bill Profile Settings, theme, account From any screen Notifications Opens the reorder advice Dukaan Mitra Floating chat button 22\n\nSlide 23: ARCHITECTURE How the pieces connect ANDROID APP Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, MVVM, Retrofit → PHP API Token auth, per-shop data, import, insights → MYSQL Products, bills, users, alerts AI LAYER Ollama (Qwen2.5 7B) and Gemini PUSH ALERTS Firebase Cloud Messaging EMAIL DIGEST PHPMailer 23\n\nSlide 24: DESIGN Bold Outline style Cream #FFF4DC Ink #0B1230 Blue #2B49D8 Yellow #FFC93C Low stock #FF9F5A Alert #E5484D Thick ink outlines and hard shadows give clear, tappable shapes. Each product category has its own colour and icon. Light, Dark and System themes, with matching palettes. 24\n\nSlide 25: AI ASSISTANT Dukaan Mitra UNDERSTANDS Shop questions in English, Hindi and Tamil. ANSWERS Uses the shop\'s own database for every number. STAYS HONEST If there is no data, it says so. EXAMPLE QUESTIONS What should I reorder this week? Which products are not selling? How much money is stuck in slow stock? 25\n\nSlide 26: TESTING How we tested AUTOMATED More than 20 backend test suites Android unit tests Import edge cases: Excel decimals, zero stock, typos HANDS-ON Real phones, small and large screens Light and dark themes Demo shop: 30 products, 73 bills, 30 days BUGS FOUND AND FIXED Excel import read every product as unknown Theme reset to System in Settings Text squeezed on small screens Chatbot said \"well stocked\" for an empty shop USABILITY STUDY [Add number of users, tasks and findings] 26\n\nSlide 27: COMPONENTS Main building blocks Module What it does Auth Sign up, login, lockout after repeated failures Inventory Products, categories, icons, stock levels Import CSV and Excel, column matching, preview Sales Bills that update stock Insights Reorder, slow and dead stock, bundles Alerts Push notifications and email digest Dukaan Mitra Chat assistant over shop data Settings Theme, account, store details 27\n\nSlide 28: LEARNING What I learned DATA Real data is messy. Import needs previews, warnings and safe defaults. AI An assistant must be honest. Numbers come from the database, never invented. TESTING Real phones find layout bugs that emulators miss. DESIGN Design for small screens first. Strong outlines keep cards clear. SAFETY Never change stock silently. Ask the user and show a preview. PROCESS AI-assisted coding is fast, but every change needs careful review. 28\n\nSlide 29: PATENT IDEA Draft concept PROBLEM Stock tools give advice without reasons, and chat assistants can invent numbers. IDEA (DRAFT CLAIMS) Explainable stock advice that shows its source numbers. Assistant that says \"no data\" instead of guessing. Import that previews stock changes before saving. Clearance and bundle ideas from the shop\'s own sales. STATUS Concept only. Not filed. Novelty not checked. DOCUMENT [Paste Drive link] 29\n\nSlide 30: NEXT STEPS What comes next # Step 1 Host the backend with HTTPS 2 Pilot with one or two real supermarkets 3 Schedule the alert and digest jobs 4 Add expiry-date tracking 5 Release build, signing and Play Store listing 30\n\nSlide 31: COMPLIANCE Before public release GOOGLE PLAY Follow Play policies. Complete the Data safety form. PRIVACY Publish a privacy policy. Review India\'s DPDP Act duties. USER CONTROL Delete-account option already built into the app. SECURITY Token login, separate data per shop, HTTPS before launch. Keys never go to GitHub. AI NOTICE Chat shows \"AI can make mistakes. Check important numbers.\" RELEASE Signed release build and store listing. 31\n\nSlide 32: THANK YOU Questions? StockSense: Smarter stock. Better business. [Your name] [Email] [GitHub / LinkedIn] 32','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 04:47:17','READY','Slide 3: OVERVIEW Project overview THE PROBLEM Reorders are guessed, so popular items run out. Slide 4: DOMAIN STUDY Product domain study SUMMARY StockSense is an Android app for retail inventory management. Slide 5: DOMAIN STUDY LinkedIn article Article  StockSense is an Android app that helps supermarket owners decide what to reorder, what to clear and what to bundle.','[\"DESIGN PHASE Figma designs Home Inventory Insights 19\",\"DESIGN PHASE Figma designs Product details Dukaan Mitra Alerts 20\",\"Slide\",\"Stocksense\",\"Dukaan\"]','[\"Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP StockSense Smarter stock.\",\"Slide 2: THE PROBLEM Product problem Medium-sized supermarkets run on guesswork, not data.\",\"Slide 3: OVERVIEW Project overview THE PROBLEM Reorders are guessed, so popular items run out.\",\"KEY IDEAS IN THIS DOMAIN Stock cover: how many days current stock will last.\",\"Slide 8: PLAN · 27 SEP TO 10 DEC 2026 Project plan # Phase Dates 1 Topic selection [add dates] 2 GPCU [add dates] 3 Requirement gathering [add dates] 4 Design phase using Figma [add dates] 5 Frontend [add dates] 6 Backend [add dates] 7 Integration phase [add dates] 8 Testing stage [add dates] 9 Deployment [add dates] 8\",\"Slide 23: ARCHITECTURE How the pieces connect ANDROID APP Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, MVVM, Retrofit → PHP API Token auth, per-shop data, import, insights → MYSQL Products, bills, users, alerts AI LAYER Ollama (Qwen2.5 7B) and Gemini PUSH ALERTS Firebase Cloud Messaging EMAIL DIGEST PHPMailer 23\",\"Light, Dark and System themes, with matching palettes.\",\"Check important numbers.\\\" RELEASE Signed release build and store listing.\"]','[\"Guessed reorders Orders depend on memory and gut feel.\",\"No next step Billing tools store numbers but rarely say what to do.\",\"Owners have little time to read reports.\",\"Recommendations that show the numbers behind them.\",\"Dukaan Mitra, an assistant that answers shop questions in English, Hindi and Tamil.\",\"Slow-moving vs dead stock: few sales versus none.\",\"Market basket: items customers buy together, which suits bundles.\"]','[\"Guessed reorders Orders depend on memory and gut feel.\",\"No next step Billing tools store numbers but rarely say what to do.\",\"Owners have little time to read reports.\",\"Recommendations that show the numbers behind them.\",\"Dukaan Mitra, an assistant that answers shop questions in English, Hindi and Tamil.\",\"Slow-moving vs dead stock: few sales versus none.\",\"Market basket: items customers buy together, which suits bundles.\"]','[\"REVIEW — Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP StockSense Smarter stock.\",\"APP — Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP StockSense Smarter stock.\",\"AI — AI-assisted inventory intelligence for medium-sized supermarkets.\",\"BY — BY · NAME: [Your name] · REG NO: [Reg no] · DEP: [Department]\",\"NAME — BY · NAME: [Your name] · REG NO: [Reg no] · DEP: [Department]\",\"REG — BY · NAME: [Your name] · REG NO: [Reg no] · DEP: [Department]\"]','[Your name] [Email] [GitHub / LinkedIn] 32',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(53,27,'kishore_Clinical_Report_20261118_130045.pdf','PDF','429.4 KB','uploads/documents/430b932fc08620de42b067aa_kishore_Clinical_Report_20261118_130045.pdf','Document','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,3,'','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 04:55:23','READY','kishore_Clinical_Report_20261118_130045.pdf is a PDF document securely stored in IntelliSpace containing 0 characters.','[\"No distinct subtopics or section headings identified in this document.\"]','[\"The document contains minimal text without distinct key point statements.\"]','[\"No quantitative metrics, analytical findings, or statistical observations identified in this document.\"]','[\"No quantitative metrics, analytical findings, or statistical observations identified in this document.\"]','[\"No specialized technical terms or definitions detected in this document.\"]','In conclusion, kishore_Clinical_Report_20261118_130045.pdf provides a complete PDF reference record structured across 1 core informational areas.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(54,1,'Natural-Language-Processing-for-Multilingual-Knowledge-Systems-Updated.pptx','PPTX','3.0 MB','uploads/documents/c38e9418d32aec52d2e542fc_Natural-Language-Processing-for-Multilingual-Knowledge-Systems-Updated.pptx','Research Paper','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,15,'Slide 1: Natural Language Processing for Multilingual Knowledge Systems Bridging Language Barriers for Inclusive Knowledge Access Knowledge is abundant — but access remains limited by language. NLP offers a path to systems where people can search, understand, and interact with information in the language they are most comfortable with. CONFERENCE PAPER PRESENTATION DEEBIKA R.B  |  VISHALI J B.Sc. Artificial Intelligence & Data Science Saveetha College of Liberal Arts and Science\n\nSlide 2: Introduction & Background NLP Enables computers to understand, process, and generate human language Multilingual NLP Extends language processing capabilities across multiple languages and scripts Multilingual Knowledge System (MKS) Stores, retrieves, and presents information across languages — combining NLP, translation, retrieval, and QA Direct translation alone loses context, cultural meaning, and domain-specific terminology — intelligent multilingual systems are essential.\n\nSlide 3: The Problem How can we develop intelligent knowledge systems that allow users to access, search, and understand information across multiple languages while preserving meaning, context, and domain-specific knowledge? Core Challenges Language barriers in accessing digital knowledge Limited NLP resources for low-resource languages Translation errors and loss of context Different writing systems and linguistic structures Ambiguous words and expressions Domain-specific terminology difficult to translate Fragmented knowledge across languages Core Problem: Same knowledge → different languages → different representations → difficult access and understanding\n\nSlide 4: Research Gap & Objectives What Existing Systems Miss Machine Translation Loses context and cultural meaning Keyword Search Fails with multilingual queries Monolingual Knowledge Bases Limited language accessibility Rule-Based NLP Difficult to scale across languages Generic LLMs Inconsistent for low-resource languages What We Need A system that can understand → translate → retrieve → connect → explain knowledge across languages. Primary Objective Develop a multilingual knowledge-processing framework enabling language-independent access to information. Key Capabilities Automatic language identification and semantic understanding Multilingual retrieval with context-preserving translation Support for low-resource language users\n\nSlide 5: Proposed Solution: Multilingual NLP Pipeline Instead of separate systems per language, the architecture creates a shared semantic representation of knowledge . Queries in different languages map to the same underlying concept. Understanding Multilingual embeddings → shared space Response Answer gen → translate → user reply Input User query → language ID → preprocess Knowledge Cross-lingual retrieval → vector store The pipeline maps diverse language inputs to a unified semantic layer, enabling cross-lingual retrieval and generation without language-specific silos. Example: English \"How can farmers reduce water consumption?\" and Tamil \"விவசாயிகள் நீர் பயன்பாட்டை எவ்வாறு குறைக்கலாம்?\" both map to the same knowledge concept.\n\nSlide 6: System Architecture & Technologies Core Technologies Multilingual Transformers: mBERT, XLM-R, Indic language models Neural Machine Translation for cross-lingual transfer Sentence Embeddings in shared semantic space Vector Databases for scalable retrieval RAG for grounded, context-aware generation Large Language Models for multilingual QA\n\nSlide 7: NLP Techniques at Each Stage Language Identification Detects input language — Tamil, Hindi, English, Telugu, and more Tokenization & Normalization Breaks text into units; standardizes across scripts Multilingual Embeddings Maps languages into a shared semantic space Named Entity Recognition Identifies people, places, organizations, dates, and technical terms Machine Translation Converts content across languages while preserving meaning Semantic Search & RAG Retrieves by meaning, not keywords; generates grounded responses\n\nSlide 8: Real-Time Example: Agricultural Knowledge Assistant The Scenario A Tamil-speaking farmer asks: \"நெற்பயிரில் பூச்சி தாக்குதலை எவ்வாறு கட்டுப்படுத்துவது?\" \"How can pest attacks in rice crops be controlled?\" The system identifies Tamil, retrieves multilingual agricultural knowledge, and responds in Tamil. The same knowledge is accessible in Hindi, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam, and English. One knowledge base → Multiple languages → Wider accessibility\n\nSlide 9: Applications, Challenges & Future Scope Applications Healthcare: Regional-language medical information Agriculture: Local-language farming guidance Education: Multilingual learning resources Legal & Government: Accessible public services Digital Libraries: Cross-language research search Conversational AI: Multilingual assistants Challenges Low-resource language datasets and code-mixing Domain-specific terminology and cultural context Bias in training data and hallucination risk Lack of standardized multilingual benchmarks Evaluation BLEU/COMET · Precision/Recall/MRR · F1 Score · Human evaluation for relevance and factuality Future Directions Voice-based systems, expanded language coverage, multimodal knowledge, personalized multilingual education, and domain-specific AI\n\nSlide 10: Conclusion Language Should Not Be a Barrier Multilingual NLP enables systems to understand, retrieve, and generate information across languages Shared Semantic Layer A unified knowledge representation connects information expressed in different languages Technologies That Enable This Multilingual Transformers, embeddings, NMT, semantic search, and RAG make it possible Real-World Impact Improved accessibility across education, agriculture, healthcare, government, and digital libraries \"One Knowledge Base. Multiple Languages. Equal Access to Information.\"\n\nSlide 11: Dataset & Preprocessing Multilingual Data Sources Parallel corpora: Samanantar, OPUS for English–Indic translation Knowledge text: Wikipedia and government portals in Tamil, Hindi, Telugu Domain content: Agriculture, healthcare, and education documents Benchmarks: FLORES-200 and IndicXTREME for evaluation Crowd input: Real user queries, including code-mixed text Preprocessing Steps Cleaning: Remove noise, duplicates, and broken encodings Normalization: Unicode normalization across scripts Tokenization: SentencePiece subword units for all languages Chunking: Split long documents into retrievable passages Tagging: Language ID and domain labels per chunk Clean, script-aware preprocessing is the foundation — poor tokenization of Indic scripts directly reduces retrieval and translation quality.\n\nSlide 12: Implementation Workflow 01 Collect & Prepare Gather multilingual text, clean it, and split into passages with language and domain metadata. 02 Embed & Index Encode passages with XLM-R or LaBSE embeddings and store them in a vector database such as FAISS. 03 Retrieve & Generate Embed the user query, fetch top-k passages across languages, and generate a grounded answer with RAG. 04 Translate & Deliver Translate the answer into the user\'s language with NMT and return it with source references. Query (any language) → shared embedding space → relevant knowledge → answer in the user\'s own language\n\nSlide 13: Evaluation Metrics & Methodology Automatic Metrics Translation: BLEU, chrF++, and COMET for meaning preservation Retrieval: Precision@k, Recall@k, and Mean Reciprocal Rank Question answering: Exact Match and F1 Score Language ID: Accuracy across scripts and code-mixed text Human Evaluation Relevance: Does the answer address the question asked? Factuality: Is the answer supported by retrieved sources? Fluency: Is the output natural in the target language? Usability: Feedback from native speakers and domain users Comparison Baselines Keyword search, translate-then-search pipelines, and monolingual retrieval compared against the proposed shared-embedding approach. Expected Outcome Higher cross-lingual retrieval accuracy and more faithful answers than keyword or translate-first systems, especially for low-resource languages.\n\nSlide 14: Ethics, Fairness & Inclusivity Responsible AI Concerns Language bias: High-resource languages dominate training data Hallucination: Fluent but incorrect answers in critical domains Privacy: Protecting user queries and personal data Cultural sensitivity: Respecting dialects, idioms, and local context Digital divide: Low literacy and limited connectivity Mitigation Strategies Grounded answers: RAG with cited, verified sources Balanced data: Community-built datasets for low-resource languages Human review: Expert checks for health and legal content Transparency: Show confidence and original source language Accessibility: Voice and low-bandwidth interfaces Inclusive access means every language community receives accurate, safe, and culturally appropriate knowledge.\n\nSlide 15: Future Scope & Roadmap Short Term Expand Coverage Add more Indian languages and dialects, improve code-mixed query handling, and fine-tune embeddings on domain data. Mid Term Voice & Multimodal Integrate speech recognition and text-to-speech, plus image and document understanding for farmers and rural users. Long Term Inclusive Knowledge Network Deploy mobile and offline-first assistants with community feedback loops and personalized multilingual learning. Goal: a scalable, voice-enabled multilingual knowledge ecosystem that reaches every community in its own language.','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 07:49:06','READY','Slide 1: Natural Language Processing for Multilingual Knowledge Systems Bridging Language Barriers for Inclusive Knowledge Access Knowledge is abundant — but access remains limited by language. NLP offers a path to systems where people can search, understand, and interact with information in the language they are most comfortable with. CONFERENCE PAPER PRESENTATION DEEBIKA R.B | VISHALI J B.Sc.','[\"Slide\",\"Multilingual\",\"Knowledge\",\"Language\",\"Translation\"]','[\"Slide 1: Natural Language Processing for Multilingual Knowledge Systems Bridging Language Barriers for Inclusive Knowledge Access Knowledge is abundant — but access remains limited by language.\",\"NLP offers a path to systems where people can search, understand, and interact with information in the language they are most comfortable with.\",\"Slide 3: The Problem How can we develop intelligent knowledge systems that allow users to access, search, and understand information across multiple languages while preserving meaning, context, and domain-specific knowledge?\",\"Primary Objective Develop a multilingual knowledge-processing framework enabling language-independent access to information.\",\"Key Capabilities Automatic language identification and semantic understanding Multilingual retrieval with context-preserving translation Support for low-resource language users\",\"Slide 5: Proposed Solution: Multilingual NLP Pipeline Instead of separate systems per language, the architecture creates a shared semantic representation of knowledge .\",\"Slide 6: System Architecture & Technologies Core Technologies Multilingual Transformers: mBERT, XLM-R, Indic language models Neural Machine Translation for cross-lingual transfer Sentence Embeddings in shared semantic space Vector Databases for scalable retrieval RAG for grounded, context-aware generation Large Language Models for multilingual QA\",\"Expected Outcome Higher cross-lingual retrieval accuracy and more faithful answers than keyword or translate-first systems, especially for low-resource languages.\"]','[\"Understanding Multilingual embeddings → shared space Response Answer gen → translate → user reply Input User query → language ID → preprocess Knowledge Cross-lingual retrieval → vector store The pipeline maps diverse language inputs to a unified semantic layer, enabling cross-lingual retrieval and generation without language-specific silos.\",\"Example: English \\\"How can farmers reduce water consumption?\\\" and Tamil \\\"விவசாயிகள் நீர் பயன்பாட்டை எவ்வாறு குறைக்கலாம்?\\\" both map to the same knowledge concept.\",\"Usability: Feedback from native speakers and domain users Comparison Baselines Keyword search, translate-then-search pipelines, and monolingual retrieval compared against the proposed shared-embedding approach.\",\"Mid Term Voice & Multimodal Integrate speech recognition and text-to-speech, plus image and document understanding for farmers and rural users.\",\"Long Term Inclusive Knowledge Network Deploy mobile and offline-first assistants with community feedback loops and personalized multilingual learning.\"]','[\"Understanding Multilingual embeddings → shared space Response Answer gen → translate → user reply Input User query → language ID → preprocess Knowledge Cross-lingual retrieval → vector store The pipeline maps diverse language inputs to a unified semantic layer, enabling cross-lingual retrieval and generation without language-specific silos.\",\"Example: English \\\"How can farmers reduce water consumption?\\\" and Tamil \\\"விவசாயிகள் நீர் பயன்பாட்டை எவ்வாறு குறைக்கலாம்?\\\" both map to the same knowledge concept.\",\"Usability: Feedback from native speakers and domain users Comparison Baselines Keyword search, translate-then-search pipelines, and monolingual retrieval compared against the proposed shared-embedding approach.\",\"Mid Term Voice & Multimodal Integrate speech recognition and text-to-speech, plus image and document understanding for farmers and rural users.\",\"Long Term Inclusive Knowledge Network Deploy mobile and offline-first assistants with community feedback loops and personalized multilingual learning.\"]','[\"NLP — NLP offers a path to systems where people can search, understand, and interact with information in the language they are most comfortable wi\",\"PAPER — CONFERENCE PAPER PRESENTATION DEEBIKA R.B | VISHALI J B.Sc.\",\"MKS — Technical acronym identified in Natural-Language-Processing-for-Multilingual-Knowledge-Systems-Updated.pptx\",\"QA — Slide 6: System Architecture & Technologies Core Technologies Multilingual Transformers: mBERT, XLM-R, Indic language models Neural Machine \",\"ID — Understanding Multilingual embeddings → shared space Response Answer gen → translate → user reply Input User query → language ID → preproces\",\"XLM — Slide 6: System Architecture & Technologies Core Technologies Multilingual Transformers: mBERT, XLM-R, Indic language models Neural Machine \"]','Slide 15: Future Scope & Roadmap Short Term Expand Coverage Add more Indian languages and dialects, improve code-mixed query handling, and fine-tune embeddings on domain data.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(55,1,'10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf','PDF','614.3 KB','uploads/documents/f2d202de46a76e5b56ef8bec_10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf','General','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,2,'MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE Simple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine Shared by Dr. Sindhuja | Anesthesiologist, Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist Migraine is more than \"just a headache\". It often comes with throbbing pain, nausea, and sensitivity to light and sound. The good news: small, steady lifestyle habits can reduce how often it strikes. Here is your quick guide. 1 Stay Hydrated Sip water regularly through the day Avoid long periods without fluids Drink more in hot weather or exercise Carry a water bottle with you 2 Don\'t Skip Meals Keep regular meal timings Avoid long gaps between meals Keep a healthy snack handy Do not start th e day on an empty stomach 3 Maintain Good Sleep Fixed sleep and wake - up time Avoid frequently changing your schedule Give your body enough rest Switch off screens before bed 4 Know Your Personal Triggers Keep a simple migraine diary and note down: What you ate Water intake Sleep duration Stress level Screen exposure Time headache started How long it lasted Date Food / Water Sleep \\(hrs\\ Stress \\(1 - 5\\ Started / Lasted Common triggers to watch for: Dehydration Skipped meals Poor / irregular sleep Stress & anxiety Long screen time Bright light / loud noise Strong smells Too much caffeine Weather change Hormonal changes \\(in women\\ 5 What To Do During an Attack Rest Lie down in a quiet, dark room if light or sound worsens symptoms Hydrate Sip water slowly and stay hydrated Medicine Follow only the plan prescribed by your doctor Avoid triggers Stay away from your known personal triggers GO TO EMERGENCY IMMEDIATELY IF YOU HAVE Sudden, very severe \"worst ever\" headache Weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking Fever with neck stiffness Sudden vision loss, confusion, or fainting Headache after a head injury Helpful habits Practise relaxation: deep breathing, yoga, meditation Take screen breaks \\(every 20 - 30 minutes\\ Gentle regular exercise like walking Limit caffeine, and have it at fixed times Try to avoid Skipping breakfast or lunch Late - night scrolling and irregular slee p Self - medicating with painkillers again and again Ignoring early warning signs \\(aura, nausea, light sensitivity\\ 6 When To See a Doctor Seek medical evaluation if your migraines are: Becoming more frequent Becoming more severe Interfering with your daily activities Needing painkillers more than 2 - 3 days a week \\(overuse can worsen headaches\\ Need personal advice? Consult the doctor. Dr. Sindhuja Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist Phone: 9361366109 Palaniappa Hospital, Ramapuram, Chennai Important: Migraine triggers differ from person to person. This guide is for general education and does not replace a medical consultation.','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 07:49:41','READY','MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE Simple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine Shared by Dr. Sindhuja | Anesthesiologist, Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist Migraine is more than \"just a headache\". It often comes with throbbing pain, nausea, and sensitivity to light and sound.','[\"Avoid\",\"Migraine\",\"Keep\",\"Sleep\",\"Stress\"]','[\"MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE Simple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine Shared by Dr.\",\"Sindhuja | Anesthesiologist, Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist Migraine is more than \\\"just a headache\\\".\",\"It often comes with throbbing pain, nausea, and sensitivity to light and sound.\",\"The good news: small, steady lifestyle habits can reduce how often it strikes.\",\"Here is your quick guide.\",\"Consult the doctor.\",\"Sindhuja Interventional Pain & Regenerative Specialist Phone: 9361366109 Palaniappa Hospital, Ramapuram, Chennai Important: Migraine triggers differ from person to person.\",\"This guide is for general education and does not replace a medical consultation.\"]','[\"No quantitative metrics, analytical findings, or statistical observations identified in this document.\"]','[\"No quantitative metrics, analytical findings, or statistical observations identified in this document.\"]','[\"CARE — MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE Simple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine Shared by Dr.\",\"GUIDE — MIGRAINE CARE GUIDE Simple daily habits to prevent and manage migraine Shared by Dr.\",\"GO — Technical acronym identified in 10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf\",\"TO — Technical acronym identified in 10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf\",\"IF — Technical acronym identified in 10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf\",\"YOU — Technical acronym identified in 10203503014675cbae03f295_Migraine_Care_Guide.pdf\"]','This guide is for general education and does not replace a medical consultation.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(57,18,'DiaWell_Presentation_tharun252514010.pptx','PPTX','8.0 MB','uploads/documents/fb930392bc9cf108bf7fba14_DiaWell_Presentation_tharun252514010.pptx','Document','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,29,'Slide 1: PROJECT PRESENTATION DiaWell Eat Smart. Track Better. Live Well. AI-powered diabetes diet management and medication reminder system Name  : Tharun J Reg no  : 252514010 Department  : B.Sc Artificial Intelligence and Data Science Timeline  : 28 September – 10 December 2026 tharunjagan47@gmail.com linkedin.com/in/tharun-j-804546442\n\nSlide 2: Product Problem & Solution THE PROBLEM Generic diet advice Most apps ignore Indian meals and the user’s latest glucose. Slow manual logging Typing every meal and its nutrients is tedious, so people stop. Missed medication One-shot alarms fire once and doses get forgotten. Privacy worries Cloud AI tools receive sensitive health data. OUR SOLUTION Snap Food vision AI Photograph a meal to get calories, macros and a health score. South Indian diet engine Daily rotating, glucose-aware, diabetic-friendly meals. Exact daily reminders Self-rescheduling alarms with Taken / Skip tracking. 100% local AI Ollama models run on your machine. Data stays private. 2\n\nSlide 3: Project Overview 3 Local AI models via Ollama 70% South Indian meals in the daily mix 5 Core modules Home · Diet · Meds · Reports · personalized AI 0 Hardcoded nutrition values Snap Food is fully AI-calculated WHAT DIAWELL DOES DiaWell is a privacy-first Android app that guides people with Type 2 diabetes through the day. It logs glucose, recognises meals from a photo, recommends South Indian diabetic-friendly foods, rings exact medication reminders and answers health questions with an AI assistant that has read the user’s own logs. BUILT WITH Kotlin Jetpack Compose Material 3 PHP MySQL Ollama 3\n\nSlide 4: Product Domain Study SUMMARY DiaWell is an Android app for people with Type 2 diabetes. It brings glucose logging, diet guidance, medication reminders, activity tracking and an AI health assistant into one place. Personal data such as glucose logs, meals and medicines tailors the advice, and the AI runs locally to protect privacy. ARTICLE India has an estimated 101 million people living with diabetes (ICMR-INDIAB study, 2023). Managing it is a daily routine: check glucose, eat suitable meals, take medicines on time and stay active. Most apps cover only one of these and few understand Indian food. DiaWell joins them and suggests meals like ragi idli, pesarattu and sundal. CONCLUSION DiaWell turns daily diabetes self-care into a simple, guided routine. By combining vision AI, a personal health assistant and dependable reminders, all running locally, it helps users eat better, stay consistent and share clear reports with their doctor. Source: ICMR–INDIAB study, The Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology, 2023. 4\n\nSlide 5: Problem Statement People managing Type 2 diabetes need one simple, private tool to log glucose, choose suitable Indian meals and never miss a dose. Meal logging is slow Typing food names and nutrients by hand takes too long, so logs stay empty. Reminders get missed A one-shot alarm rings once. After a reboot or a skipped dose it never returns. Reports Difficult for regular glucose logging and report generation Data leaves the phone Cloud AI services receive glucose, food and medication details. 5\n\nSlide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE Designer and developer of DiaWell, covering the full pipeline: the Android app, the PHP + MySQL backend and the Ollama-based local AI features. 28 Sep – 10 Dec 2026 Project timeline MY RESPONSIBILITIES Design the app UI/UX in an Obsidian / Royal Purple theme with dark and light modes Build the Android app in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose Create PHP + MySQL endpoints for logs, medicines and reports Integrate local Ollama models for Snap Food, DIVA and RAG Build the daily diet engine and exact medication alarms Test on device and export PDF clinical records 6\n\nSlide 7: Project Plan Phase Wk 1 28 Sep Wk 2 5 Oct Wk 3 12 Oct Wk 4 19 Oct Wk 5 26 Oct Wk 6 2 Nov Wk 7 9 Nov Wk 8 16 Nov Wk 9 23 Nov Wk 10 30 Nov Wk 11 10 Dec Concept, Research & Planning UI/UX & Theme Design Android Frontend (Compose) PHP + MySQL Backend Local AI: Snap Food, DIVA, RAG Diet Engine & Medication Alarms Testing, Reports & Polish Documentation & Final Demo Planned schedule · 11 weeks from 28 September to 10 December 2026 7\n\nSlide 8: User Personas (2 of 2) Madan SD 18 · Student · type 2 diabetes · Food tracking FRUSTRATIONS Does not know which everyday foods push his sugar up Typing every meal into an app feels like a chore Wants to act early so prediabetes never becomes diabetes GOAL Track every meal with one photo and build food habits that keep sugar in range and prevent diabetes. Nitesh MV 19 · Student · Prediabetic · Food tracking FRUSTRATIONS College and outside meals make carbs hard to judge Forgets to log meals and glucose checks Needs simple guidance, not complex medical charts GOAL See calories, carbs and a health score at a glance and stay on track to avoid diabetes. Target users: students using DiaWell for prediabetes prevention and food tracking. 8\n\nSlide 9: User Journey Map Persona: , madan,18,student |   Goal: eat well, log easily and never miss a dose ACTION TASK LIST FEELING IMPROVEMENT OPPORTUNITY Sign up & set profile a. Create an account  b. Choose diabetes type, glucose target, allergies and Veg / Non-Veg Hopeful and in control Short onboarding walkthrough Log glucose a. Open Log Glucose  b. Enter value and reading type  c. Save Informed Import from CGM or wearables Snap a meal a. Open Snap Food  b. Take or upload a photo  c. Adjust servings, tap Done Impressed, saves typing Higher accuracy for mixed dishes Follow the diet plan a. Read the AI Food Recommendation  b. Tap Try Another Confident More regional cuisines Take medicines a. Alarm rings at the exact time  b. Tap Taken or Skip Reassured Caregiver alerts for missed doses Share with doctor a. Open Export Clinical Records  b. Choose range and sections  c. Share PDF Prepared Direct sharing with clinics 9\n\nSlide 10: Competitive Analysis Competitor Strengths Limitations DiaWell’s differentiator HealthifyMe Large food database, photo food logging and coaching. General fitness focus; mostly cloud-based; advanced coaching is paid. Diabetes-first design, local AI, glucose-aware South Indian meal engine. mySugr Strong glucose and insulin logging. Little meal guidance and no Indian food focus. Joins glucose logs with AI diet recommendations. Medisafe Reliable medication reminders. No diet advice and no glucose-aware guidance. Reminders, diet, glucose and AI in one app. Cloud AI chatbots Fluent general health answers. Do not know your logs; data leaves the device. DIVA reads your own logs through RAG, fully local. Comparison based on each product’s publicly described core features. 10\n\nSlide 11: Business Potential 101M people estimated to be living with diabetes in India ICMR–INDIAB study, The Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology, 2023 WHO CAN USE DIAWELL People with Type 2 diabetes Daily logging, meals and reminders Family caregivers Understand the routine of a loved one Clinics and diabetologists Doctor-ready PDF and CSV records Dietitians and wellness coaches South Indian meal guidance to build on Why it stands out: local AI means privacy and no per-request cloud cost, and the diet engine is built around Indian food. 11\n\nSlide 12: Tech Stack & Local AI Architecture Android App Kotlin + Jetpack Compose Obsidian / Royal Purple theme Dark and light modes Material 3 vector icons Local Backend PHP on XAMPP MySQL database ADB reverse routing ngrok headers Ollama (local) qwen2.5vl:3b Vision AI · Snap Food qwen2.5:3b Chat LLM · DIVA nomic-embed-text Embeddings · RAG 100% local, privacy-first AI Food photos, glucose logs and chat history never leave the user’s own machine: every AI call is served by Ollama. 12\n\nSlide 13: App Flow Diagram Splash Login / Create Account Patient Profile (Step 1) Health Preferences (Step 2) Home Dashboard BOTTOM NAVIGATION Home Daily wellness & streak Key health metrics Log Glucose · Log Meal DIVA tip · AI Activity Coach Diet Snap Food (vision AI) Serving stepper · health score Food Log AI food recommendation Meds Add / set reminder Medicine catalog (70,000+) Exact alarm · Taken · Snooze · Skip Reports Weekly report Glucose history (7d · 30d · 3m) Export PDF / CSV Settings Profile & photo Notifications Privacy & security App lock · biometrics 13 LOCAL AI LAYER (OLLAMA) · POWERS EVERY TAB DIVA AI chat Voice mode · RAG · qwen2.5:3b Snap Food Vision AI · qwen2.5vl:3b Diet engine Daily rotating · 70% South Indian Activity Coach MET intensity · glucose-aware RAG memory nomic-embed-text logs\n\nSlide 14: Figma Product Sketches (1 of 2) FIGMA DESIGN PROCESS 14\n\nSlide 15: Figma Product Sketches (2 of 2) FIGMA DESIGN PROCESS 15\n\nSlide 16: App Screens: Onboarding Splash Login Patient profile · Step 1 Health preferences · Step 2 16\n\nSlide 17: Home, Activity Coach & Streaks Home dashboard AI Activity Coach Streak reward HOME Wellness score, logging streak and glucose target Key metrics: glucose, nutrition, medication, weekly report DIVA tip of the day ACTIVITY COACH Walking, cycling or running with MET intensity Goal timer, distance, calories and steps AI rationale based on current glucose STREAKS Celebrates consecutive logging days Quick Log Glucose and Log Meal buttons 17\n\nSlide 18: Snap Food: Vision AI Diet & Nutrition Snap Food scanner 1 Snap or upload Take a photo with the camera or pick one from the gallery. 2 Optimise Image resized to 512 px; the model is silently pre-warmed when the screen opens. 3 Analyse qwen2.5vl:3b returns food items, calories, protein, fat, carbs, fibre, a 1–10 health score and sub-item breakdown. 4 Adjust The − / + serving stepper recalculates every value. 5 Done One tap updates the Diet Log and the Home dashboard. Zero hardcoded values · model kept warm with keep_alive 30m Meal breakdown 18\n\nSlide 19: Glucose Tracking GLUCOSE HISTORY 7 days, 30 days or 3 months of trend Average, lowest and total readings Status chips: Elevated, In target, High LOG GLUCOSE Quick values: 65 Low · 110 Target · 155 Elevated · 195 High Reading type: Fasting, Before / After meal, Bedtime, Random Date, time and optional notes Hands-free: say “Log fasting sugar 115” to DIVA Glucose History Log Glucose 19\n\nSlide 20: Exact Daily Medication Reminders Your medications Medicine catalog HOW EACH REMINDER WORKS 1 Schedule Pick a medicine from 70,000+ Indian medicines or add your own 2 Alarm fires Exact alarm via setAlarmClock at the chosen time 3 Taken / Skip The user responds from the notification 4 Reschedule Tomorrow’s alarm is set for the same time automatically Upgrade: replaced the one-shot Android alarm with self-rescheduling exact alarms plus a BootReceiver, so reminders survive reboots. Medication alarm 20\n\nSlide 21: DIVA: AI Health Assistant DIVA chat DIVA voice mode RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED ANSWERS (RAG) Your logs Glucose, diet, activity, medication nomic-embed-text Embeds and retrieves relevant logs qwen2.5:3b Writes the personalised answer Personal: reads your own glucose, diet, activity and medication context before answering. Conversational: ask “What is my glucose level?” or “What medications am I taking?”. Voice mode: hands-free commands such as “Log fasting sugar 115” or “Remind Metformin at 8 PM”. Private: chat and embeddings are served locally by Ollama. 21\n\nSlide 22: Reports & Export WEEKLY REPORT Glucose overview with weekly average and time in range Meals logged and average daily calories Medication reminder adherence EXPORT CLINICAL RECORDS Range: 7 days, 30 days, 3 months or all time Format: hospital-grade PDF or spreadsheet CSV Pick sections: glucose, medication, diet, activity Compiles real MySQL logs into a doctor-ready summary Weekly report Export Clinical Records Exported PDF report (sample) 22\n\nSlide 23: Settings, Privacy & Notifications PERSONAL PROFILE Photo options and personal details Diabetes type and contact info NOTIFICATIONS Medication, meal and glucose reminders Smart health nudges, weekly alerts DIVA voice, vibration, quiet hours PRIVACY & SECURITY App lock and biometric unlock Anonymised-data toggle, export, delete account Personal profile Notifications Privacy & security 23\n\nSlide 24: Daily Rotating South Indian Diet Engine DAILY MEAL MIX INPUTS Latest glucose Allergies Veg / Non-Veg Rotation engine Non-repeating daily rotation, fresh every day, matched to the user’s health profile OUTPUT: AI FOOD RECOMMENDATION FOR YOUR HEALTH Ragi Idli Pesarattu Thinai Sambar Sundal Plus a Try Another button for a fresh suggestion. 24\n\nSlide 25: Challenges Solved Reminders BEFORE Android one-shot alarm rang once and stopped. AFTER Self-rescheduling exact daily alarms (setAlarmClock) plus BootReceiver. Snap Food speed BEFORE Vision model felt slow on every photo. AFTER Single-pass warm model (keep_alive 30m), 512 px images, silent pre-warm. Generates reports BEFORE difficult for regular checkup and report AFTER generates reports based on the users diabetic health Food suggestions BEFORE Recommendations repeated and felt generic. AFTER Daily non-repeating engine: ~70% South Indian, ~30% general. 25\n\nSlide 26: List of Components Component Technology Specifications Mobile App Kotlin, Jetpack Compose Obsidian / Royal Purple theme, dark and light modes, bottom nav: Home, Diet, Meds, Reports, Settings. Backend & Database PHP (XAMPP) + MySQL Local endpoints for logs, medicines and reports; ADB reverse routing and ngrok headers. Vision AI Ollama · qwen2.5vl:3b Snap Food: items, calories, macros, fibre, health score; 512 px input, keep_alive 30m. Health Assistant Ollama · qwen2.5:3b DIVA: conversational and voice assistant using personal logs as context. RAG Memory nomic-embed-text Embeddings that retrieve glucose, diet, activity and medication logs. Diet Engine Rotating recommendation logic ~70% South Indian diabetic-friendly, ~30% general; filtered by glucose, allergies, Veg / Non-Veg. Reminder System setAlarmClock + BootReceiver Exact daily alarms that reschedule after Taken / Skip and survive reboots. Reports PDF / CSV export Doctor-ready clinical summary with glucose, regimen, meals and activity. 26\n\nSlide 27: Project Learning PROJECT IMPACT DiaWell makes everyday diabetes care simpler and more private. Photo-based food logging, a personal AI assistant, a diet engine rooted in South Indian food and reminders that never miss a day turn scattered self-care into one guided routine, and doctor-ready reports close the loop. WHAT I LEARNT Technological innovation Running vision, chat and embedding models locally with Ollama inside a mobile product. Problem-solving Exact Android alarms, model latency and rotating recommendation logic. Impact of technology Privacy-first AI can personalise health guidance without sending data to the cloud. 27\n\nSlide 28: Next Steps A Step A: Design Refinement Polish the light theme Add an onboarding walkthrough Add Tamil language support B Step B: Prototyping & Testing Usability tests with real users Improve accuracy for mixed dishes Expand the South Indian food range C Step C: Documentation & Rollout Caregiver alerts for missed doses Wearable / CGM import Direct sharing with clinics 28\n\nSlide 29: Thank You Eat Smart. Track Better. Live Well. Tharun J Reg no 252514010  ·  B.Sc Artificial Intelligence and Data Science tharunjagan47@gmail.com linkedin.com/in/tharun-j-804546442 Questions?','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-20 08:04:42','READY','Slide 3: Project Overview 3 Local AI models via Ollama 70% South Indian meals in the daily mix 5 Core modules Home · Diet · Meds · Reports · personalized AI 0 Hardcoded nutrition values Snap Food is fully AI-calculated WHAT DIAWELL DOES DiaWell is a privacy-first Android app that guides people with Type 2 diabetes through the day. Slide 4: Product Domain Study SUMMARY DiaWell is an Android app for people with Type 2 diabetes. By combining vision AI, a personal health assistant and dependable reminders, all running locally, it helps users eat better, stay consistent and share clear reports with their doctor.','[\"Figma Product Sketches (1 of 2) FIGMA DESIGN PROCESS 14\",\"Figma Product Sketches (2 of 2) FIGMA DESIGN PROCESS 15\",\"Slide\",\"Food\",\"Indian\"]','[\"AI-powered diabetes diet management and medication reminder system Name : Tharun J Reg no : 252514010 Department : B.Sc Artificial Intelligence and Data Science Timeline : 28 September – 10 December 2026 tharunjagan47@gmail.com linkedin.com\\/in\\/tharun-j-804546442\",\"100% local AI Ollama models run on your machine.\",\"Slide 3: Project Overview 3 Local AI models via Ollama 70% South Indian meals in the daily mix 5 Core modules Home · Diet · Meds · Reports · personalized AI 0 Hardcoded nutrition values Snap Food is fully AI-calculated WHAT DIAWELL DOES DiaWell is a privacy-first Android app that guides people with Type 2 diabetes through the day.\",\"Slide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE Designer and developer of DiaWell, covering the full pipeline: the Android app, the PHP + MySQL backend and the Ollama-based local AI features.\",\"Comparison based on each product’s publicly described core features.\",\"2 Optimise Image resized to 512 px; the model is silently pre-warmed when the screen opens.\",\"Zero hardcoded values · model kept warm with keep_alive 30m Meal breakdown 18\",\"AFTER Single-pass warm model (keep_alive 30m), 512 px images, silent pre-warm.\"]','[\"Exact daily reminders Self-rescheduling alarms with Taken \\/ Skip tracking.\",\"It logs glucose, recognises meals from a photo, recommends South Indian diabetic-friendly foods, rings exact medication reminders and answers health questions with an AI assistant that has read the user’s own logs.\",\"It brings glucose logging, diet guidance, medication reminders, activity tracking and an AI health assistant into one place.\",\"Personal data such as glucose logs, meals and medicines tailors the advice, and the AI runs locally to protect privacy.\",\"ARTICLE India has an estimated 101 million people living with diabetes (ICMR-INDIAB study, 2023).\",\"Most apps cover only one of these and few understand Indian food.\",\"By combining vision AI, a personal health assistant and dependable reminders, all running locally, it helps users eat better, stay consistent and share clear reports with their doctor.\"]','[\"Exact daily reminders Self-rescheduling alarms with Taken \\/ Skip tracking.\",\"It logs glucose, recognises meals from a photo, recommends South Indian diabetic-friendly foods, rings exact medication reminders and answers health questions with an AI assistant that has read the user’s own logs.\",\"It brings glucose logging, diet guidance, medication reminders, activity tracking and an AI health assistant into one place.\",\"Personal data such as glucose logs, meals and medicines tailors the advice, and the AI runs locally to protect privacy.\",\"ARTICLE India has an estimated 101 million people living with diabetes (ICMR-INDIAB study, 2023).\",\"Most apps cover only one of these and few understand Indian food.\",\"By combining vision AI, a personal health assistant and dependable reminders, all running locally, it helps users eat better, stay consistent and share clear reports with their doctor.\"]','[\"AI — AI-powered diabetes diet management and medication reminder system Name : Tharun J Reg no : 252514010 Department : B.Sc Artificial Intellige\",\"OUR — OUR SOLUTION Snap Food vision AI Photograph a meal to get calories, macros and a health score.\",\"WHAT — Slide 3: Project Overview 3 Local AI models via Ollama 70% South Indian meals in the daily mix 5 Core modules Home · Diet · Meds · Reports ·\",\"DOES — Slide 3: Project Overview 3 Local AI models via Ollama 70% South Indian meals in the daily mix 5 Core modules Home · Diet · Meds · Reports ·\",\"BUILT — BUILT WITH Kotlin Jetpack Compose Material 3 PHP MySQL Ollama 3\",\"WITH — BUILT WITH Kotlin Jetpack Compose Material 3 PHP MySQL Ollama 3\"]','Problem-solving Exact Android alarms, model latency and rotating recommendation logic.',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(58,18,'VitalSync_AI_Product_Review  final ppt.pptx','PPTX','5.6 MB','uploads/documents/fefce5a69a16bafac57fe7a4_VitalSync_AI_Product_Reviewfinalppt.pptx','Document','Internal Storage',NULL,0,0,30,'Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW  ·  ANDROID APP VitalSync AI Smarter Health. Better Living. An AI-powered Android wellness app to monitor health information, track fitness, nutrition and sleep, and receive AI-assisted wellness insights. BY Nitesh MV  ·  REG NO: 2525214025  ·  DEPT: B.Sc. AI & DS niteshmanjula886@gmail.com ·   github.com/niteshmanjula886-coder\n\nSlide 2: THE PROBLEM Product problem Managing health day to day is harder than it should be. That leads to: Scattered data Steps, vitals, sleep and meals live in separate apps, so the full picture is missing. Numbers without meaning Raw values rarely come with context, trends or a simple next step. Inconsistent habits Workouts, meals and sleep are logged in different places, or not at all. Generic guidance Quick, personal wellness answers are hard to find in one place. Based on our own study of common wellness apps; to be validated with user feedback. 2\n\nSlide 3: OVERVIEW Project overview THE PROBLEM Health data is scattered across several apps. Numbers are shown without context. Fitness, diet and sleep are tracked separately. Quick wellness guidance is hard to get. THE SOLUTION One dashboard for vitals, activity, nutrition and sleep. Workout logging with sets, reps and a rest timer. Wellness score and weekly trends at a glance. AI assistant for general wellness guidance, not diagnosis. Home dashboard · demo data 3\n\nSlide 4: DOMAIN STUDY Product domain study Vitals Heart rate, SpO₂ and blood pressure. Readings need compatible sensors or health sources. Wellness score One summary number built from tracked data. Informational only. Device data Android Health Connect brings in data from supported apps and devices. Nutrition and sleep Protein, meals, sleep hours and consistency support daily habits. SUMMARY VitalSync AI is an Android app for personal wellness tracking. It brings vitals, activity, nutrition and sleep into one place and gives general, non-diagnostic guidance. GOOD TO KNOW A smartphone alone cannot accurately measure SpO₂ or blood pressure. Values depend on compatible sensors, supported health data sources or manual entry. 4\n\nSlide 5: DOMAIN STUDY LinkedIn article ARTICLE Most of us track steps in one app, workouts in another, and meals or sleep in our heads. VitalSync AI brings these together in one Android app. Users see a daily wellness score, key vitals, workout logs and weekly trends on a single dashboard, and can ask an AI assistant for general wellness guidance. VitalSync AI does not diagnose conditions, and readings depend on compatible sensors or supported health data sources. It is an undergraduate project built with Kotlin, with more features still in development. CONCLUSION One place for your wellness data, with clear and cautious AI guidance. LINKEDIN PROFILE linkedin.com/in/niteshsukuna [Add article link after posting] 5\n\nSlide 6: PROBLEM STATEMENT What we set out to fix 1 Everyday health data is spread across several apps, so users rarely see the full picture. 2 Raw numbers often come without context, trends or a simple next step. 3 Users need one easy mobile app to track vitals, fitness, diet and sleep, with cautious AI-assisted guidance. VitalSync AI: a unified, mobile-first wellness companion for tracking and understanding personal health data. 6\n\nSlide 7: SCOPE Project scope MY ROLE Design and build VitalSync AI: the Android app, supporting backend services and the AI assistant. The goal is an app that helps users track their wellness data in one place. OUT OF SCOPE Medical diagnosis or treatment advice. Designing the app UI and dark theme in Figma Building the dashboard, vitals, gym, profile and AI screens Device integration with Android Health Connect Backend APIs and database with PHP and MySQL Integrating the AI wellness assistant Testing, refining and reviewing every change 7\n\nSlide 8: PLAN  ·  [ADD PROJECT DATES] Project plan # Phase Dates 1 Topic selection [add dates] 2 Requirement gathering [add dates] 3 UI/UX design using Figma [add dates] 4 Android frontend [add dates] 5 Backend and database [add dates] 6 Device integration (Health Connect) [add dates] 7 AI assistant integration [add dates] 8 Testing stage [add dates] 9 Deployment and release [add dates] 8\n\nSlide 9: MILESTONES Project timeline 1 [add date] Project topic chosen: VitalSync AI 2 [add date] Requirements and screens planned 3 [add date] UI designed in Figma 4 [add date] Core Android screens built 5 [add date] Backend and database connected 6 [add date] AI assistant integrated 7 [add date] Device integration (Health Connect) 8 [add date] Testing and project review 9\n\nSlide 10: USER PERSONA 1 The health-conscious user K Kishore, 22 College student who wants to build steady healthy habits ILLUSTRATIVE PERSONA GOALS Keep an eye on daily vitals, steps, sleep and water. Build steady healthy habits. PAIN POINTS Uses a different app for each metric, is unsure what numbers mean, and forgets to check them. WHAT VITALSYNC AI GIVES One dashboard with a wellness score, weekly trends and small daily steps. 10\n\nSlide 11: USER PERSONA 2 The fitness enthusiast T Tharun, 20 College gym-goer focused on strength and muscle ILLUSTRATIVE PERSONA GOALS Log workouts with sets, reps and weights. Track protein and see progress over time. PAIN POINTS Writes workouts in notes, counts protein elsewhere, and cannot see sleep next to training. WHAT VITALSYNC AI GIVES Gym tracker with training splits and rest timer, a nutrition tab, and an AI assistant for general tips. 11\n\nSlide 12: USER JOURNEY From sign-up to insight 1 Sign up USER Creates an account and logs in. VITALSYNC AI Keeps each user’s profile separate. 2 Set up profile USER Enters age, height, weight and a goal. VITALSYNC AI Personalises the dashboard. 3 Add data USER Enters readings or connects a device. VITALSYNC AI Labels each reading by its source. 4 Review USER Opens the home dashboard. VITALSYNC AI Shows score, vitals and activity. 5 Train and eat USER Logs workouts and meals. VITALSYNC AI Tracks sets, reps and nutrition. 6 Ask and improve USER Chats with the AI assistant. VITALSYNC AI Gives general guidance, not a diagnosis. 12\n\nSlide 13: COMPETITOR ANALYSIS Where VitalSync AI fits Product Strength Gap VitalSync AI targets Google Fit [verify] Activity and fitness tracking Adds gym logging, nutrition and an AI assistant in one app Fitbit [verify] Wearable-linked health tracking Aims to be device-flexible through Health Connect (planned) MyFitnessPal [verify] Food and nutrition logging Combines nutrition with vitals, sleep and workouts Samsung Health [verify] Broad tracking on Samsung devices Targets any Android phone with supported sources [verify] General descriptions only. Confirm current features against each product before presenting. 13\n\nSlide 14: MARKET POTENTIAL Why the need is real Smartphones are everywhere Android phones give a ready platform for everyday wellness tracking. Shared health data Android Health Connect offers a common way to read data from supported apps and devices. Easier guidance AI assistants make it simpler to ask general wellness questions. USER EXPERIENCE GOAL Easy to read at a glance The home screen puts the wellness score, key vitals and activity on one screen, so users see their day in seconds. USER EXPERIENCE GOAL Low effort to use Manual logs, workout sets and the AI chat take only a few taps from the bottom navigation bar. 14\n\nSlide 15: PROJECT VALUE Project value 5 core tabs Home, Vitals, AI, Profile, Gym 4 key vitals on home Heart rate, SpO₂, blood pressure, steps 10 planned modules From authentication to settings WHAT THE USER GETS A daily wellness score at a glance. Vitals with simple status labels. Weekly trends and small daily steps. Workout logging and AI guidance. Vital Signs · demo data 15\n\nSlide 16: PAIN POINTS Problems and our answers Scattered data Steps, vitals, sleep and meals live in separate apps. One dashboard Wellness score, vitals and activity on the home screen. Numbers without meaning Raw values rarely come with context or trends. Labels and trends Status labels on vitals and weekly trends in the AI tab. Separate fitness tracking Workouts and nutrition are logged in different places. Gym and nutrition Workouts, rest timer, nutrition and analytics in one tab. Hard to get guidance Personal wellness questions go unanswered. AI assistant Chat for general guidance with a “not a medical diagnosis” notice. 16\n\nSlide 17: DESIGN PROCESS Product sketches (1 of 2) Home Dashboard Vitals Dashboard Gym Screen Diet Tracker AI Chatbot REAL APP SCREENSHOTS · DEMO DATA 17\n\nSlide 18: DESIGN PROCESS Product sketches (2 of 2) Profile Screen Sleep Tracker Weekly Report Settings REAL APP SCREENSHOTS · DEMO DATA 18\n\nSlide 19: APP FLOW How the app works 1 Sign up or log in Create an account and sign in securely. 2 Set up profile Add age, height, weight and a health goal. 3 Add health data Enter readings or sync from supported sources. 4 Dashboard updates Wellness score, vitals and activity refresh. 5 Track gym and diet Log workouts, sets, reps and nutrition. 6 Review trends See weekly activity, sleep, hydration and heart rate. 7 Ask the AI Chat for general wellness guidance. 8 Reports View health history and trends over time. 19\n\nSlide 20: FLOW DIAGRAM Screen-to-screen flow Login / Sign up Bottom navigation: 5 tabs Home Wellness score, key vitals, activity and report link Vitals Heart rate, blood pressure, SpO₂, weight and BMI AI Weekly trends, small daily steps and chat assistant Profile Personal info, goals, privacy, settings and help Gym Workouts, nutrition and analytics tabs 20\n\nSlide 21: ARCHITECTURE How the pieces connect HEALTH DATA INTEGRATION UNDER DEVELOPMENT Android Health Connect Compatible health devices Manual entry ANDROID APPLICATION IMPLEMENTED Kotlin XML / Jetpack MVVM architecture BACKEND UNDER DEVELOPMENT PHP APIs Profiles, readings, auth Python AI services Assistant requests DATABASE UNDER DEVELOPMENT AI LAYER UNDER DEVELOPMENT MySQL User profiles Health readings Python Ollama / Qwen AI wellness assistant Status: IMPLEMENTED UNDER DEVELOPMENT 21\n\nSlide 22: DESIGN UI/UX design Home Vitals Gym Profile REAL SCREENSHOTS · DEMO DATA APP PALETTE (APPROX.) #0F0F0F Black #1E1E1E Card #BD86FE Purple #4BC89C Teal #E27A7B Alert Dark theme with rounded, glass-style cards. Colour-coded status: teal normal, red alert, purple AI. Bottom navigation: Home, Vitals, AI, Profile, Gym. Large, readable numbers on small screens. 22\n\nSlide 23: AI ASSISTANT AI assistant UNDERSTANDS Wellness questions typed in plain language. ANSWERS General guidance on activity, nutrition and sleep, plus weekly trend summaries. STAYS SAFE Chat shows “General wellness guidance only · Not a medical diagnosis.” It never diagnoses. EXAMPLE QUESTIONS How can I sleep better? Suggest a protein snack Summarise my week AI chat Weekly trends 23\n\nSlide 24: TESTING How we test TEST PLAN Functional checks for every module Manual testing on a real Android phone Dark theme and small-screen layout checks OBSERVED SO FAR A short query (“dosa cal”) returned a description, not calories Demo data triggers strong status labels, so wording needs review Each value must be labelled device, manual or demo PLANNED NEXT Unit tests for ViewModels and data handling Device tests with a compatible health source Safety checks on AI answers USER EXPERIENCE SUMMARY Informal testing on a real Android phone by the developer Dashboard and bottom navigation are easy to read at a glance Status wording and short AI queries need refinement A formal study with a small group of users is planned 24\n\nSlide 25: COMPONENTS Main building blocks Module What it does Status User authentication Sign up, login and personal profile Implemented Home dashboard Wellness score, key vitals and activity summary Implemented Vitals monitoring Heart rate, SpO₂, blood pressure, weight and BMI Implemented Device integration Android Health Connect for supported data sources Proposed Gym module Workout tracking, training splits and rest timer Implemented Diet module Nutrition and protein tracking Implemented Sleep module Manual sleep log and sleep history Implemented AI assistant Wellness chatbot and weekly insights Implemented Reports Weekly health report and 7-day trend Implemented Settings Account and application preferences Implemented 25\n\nSlide 26: LEARNING What I learned ANDROID Building screens in Kotlin with MVVM and a bottom-navigation layout. DESIGN Designing a dark, card-based interface that stays readable on small screens. HEALTH DATA Real sensor data needs compatible devices and a clear label for each source. AI An assistant needs safe wording, clear limits and a non-diagnostic notice. PRIVACY Health data is personal. Collect only what is needed and protect it. PROCESS Test early on real phones and review every change carefully. 26\n\nSlide 27: PATENT CONCEPT Draft concept PROBLEM Wellness data is split across tools, and chat assistants can sound like medical advice. STATUS Concept only. Not filed. Novelty not checked. IDEA (DRAFT CLAIMS) 1 A single wellness dashboard that combines vitals, activity, nutrition and sleep into one score. 2 Labelling each reading by source: device reading, manual entry or demo data. 3 An AI assistant that gives general guidance with a built-in non-diagnostic notice. 4 Device-flexible data intake through Android Health Connect. 27\n\nSlide 28: FUTURE ENHANCEMENTS What comes next # Step 1 Complete Health Connect integration with compatible devices 2 Add automatic sleep data from supported sources 3 Expand nutrition tracking with a food database 4 Extend reports with longer history and export 5 Improve the AI assistant: safety checks and better answers to short queries 6 Pilot testing with a small group of users 7 Host the backend with HTTPS and prepare a release build 28\n\nSlide 29: COMPLIANCE AND PRIVACY Before public release GOOGLE PLAY Follow Google Play policies for health apps and complete the Data safety form. PRIVACY Publish a privacy policy and review India’s DPDP Act duties before release. USER CONTROL Let users edit their profile, log out and delete their account and data. SECURITY Secure login, HTTPS for all API calls and no secret keys on GitHub. AI NOTICE Chat shows “General wellness guidance only · Not a medical diagnosis.” DATA HONESTY Label readings as device, manual or demo data. Make no medical claims. 29\n\nSlide 30: THANK YOU Questions? VitalSync AI: Smarter Health. Better Living. Nitesh MV  ·  Reg no 2525214025  ·  B.Sc. AI & DS niteshmanjula886@gmail.com github.com/niteshmanjula886-coder linkedin.com/in/niteshsukuna','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-23 03:41:57','READY','Slide 3: OVERVIEW Project overview THE PROBLEM Health data is scattered across several apps. Wellness score One summary number built from tracked data. SUMMARY VitalSync AI is an Android app for personal wellness tracking.','[\"Slide\",\"Android\",\"Vitalsync\",\"Health\",\"User\"]','[\"Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP VitalSync AI Smarter Health.\",\"BY Nitesh MV · REG NO: 2525214025 · DEPT: B.Sc.\",\"Users see a daily wellness score, key vitals, workout logs and weekly trends on a single dashboard, and can ask an AI assistant for general wellness guidance.\",\"It is an undergraduate project built with Kotlin, with more features still in development.\",\"Confirm current features against each product before presenting.\",\"USER EXPERIENCE GOAL Easy to read at a glance The home screen puts the wellness score, key vitals and activity on one screen, so users see their day in seconds.\",\"Slide 15: PROJECT VALUE Project value 5 core tabs Home, Vitals, AI, Profile, Gym 4 key vitals on home Heart rate, SpO₂, blood pressure, steps 10 planned modules From authentication to settings WHAT THE USER GETS A daily wellness score at a glance.\",\"SECURITY Secure login, HTTPS for all API calls and no secret keys on GitHub.\"]','[\"Numbers without meaning Raw values rarely come with context, trends or a simple next step.\",\"Generic guidance Quick, personal wellness answers are hard to find in one place.\",\"Numbers are shown without context.\",\"Readings need compatible sensors or health sources.\",\"Nutrition and sleep Protein, meals, sleep hours and consistency support daily habits.\",\"SUMMARY VitalSync AI is an Android app for personal wellness tracking.\",\"Values depend on compatible sensors, supported health data sources or manual entry.\"]','[\"Numbers without meaning Raw values rarely come with context, trends or a simple next step.\",\"Generic guidance Quick, personal wellness answers are hard to find in one place.\",\"Numbers are shown without context.\",\"Readings need compatible sensors or health sources.\",\"Nutrition and sleep Protein, meals, sleep hours and consistency support daily habits.\",\"SUMMARY VitalSync AI is an Android app for personal wellness tracking.\",\"Values depend on compatible sensors, supported health data sources or manual entry.\"]','[\"REVIEW — Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP VitalSync AI Smarter Health.\",\"APP — Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP VitalSync AI Smarter Health.\",\"AI — Slide 1: PRODUCT REVIEW · ANDROID APP VitalSync AI Smarter Health.\",\"BY — BY Nitesh MV · REG NO: 2525214025 · DEPT: B.Sc.\",\"MV — BY Nitesh MV · REG NO: 2525214025 · DEPT: B.Sc.\",\"REG — BY Nitesh MV · REG NO: 2525214025 · DEPT: B.Sc.\"]','AI & DS niteshmanjula886@gmail.com github.com/niteshmanjula886-coder linkedin.com/in/niteshsukuna',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(59,18,'IntelliFile_AI_Presentation_R_kishore_og.pptx','PPTX','4.6 MB','uploads/documents/eadfb9e09db83de6a09a5b03_IntelliFile_AI_Presentation_R_kishore_og.pptx','Document','Internal Storage','IMPORTANT',0,0,27,'Slide 1: INTELLIFILE AI Find. Prioritize. Access. IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R. KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\n\nSlide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date. Finding the right file on time is slow, and important files get buried. Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists. No Prioritization: Urgent and low-value files look the same. Scattered Files: Downloads, WhatsApp and browser files end up in different places. Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents. Solution AI Smart Search: Find files with natural-language questions. AI Prioritization: Mark documents Important, Normal or Low. AI Vault: Index selected documents for AI analysis and insights. Privacy by Design: Only documents are accessed, and only with consent.\n\nSlide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails. Important documents (IDs, policies, assignments) get lost among 100+ other files. Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data. IntelliFile finds files using natural language, e.g. “find Kishore ppt”. Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters. The AI Vault indexes chosen documents and shows AI Insights. Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\n\nSlide 4: Product domain study SUMMARY: IntelliFile AI is an AI-powered document management app for Android. It scans documents on the device (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV and more), shows them in one organised place, and lets users search with plain language. Each document can be marked Important, Normal or Low, saved for quick access, or moved to the AI Vault where it is indexed for AI analysis. Unlike ordinary file managers, IntelliFile focuses on finding the right document quickly and on keeping urgent files visible, while only accessing documents and never photos or media without consent. ARTICLE: Digital documents pile up fast on a student’s or professional’s phone. IntelliFile AI turns that pile into an organised , searchable library. Its AI assistant answers requests like “find my Kishore files” across Device Files and the AI Vault, while a priority dashboard shows how many documents are Important, Normal or Low. CONCLUSION: IntelliFile AI brings search, prioritization and privacy together in one simple app. By helping users find, prioritize and access files easily, it saves time and reduces the stress of lost or forgotten documents\n\nSlide 5: Problem Statement Existing file managers list documents only by name and date, so finding the right file in 100+ documents takes too long. Users cannot easily tell which documents are urgent, which are routine, and which can be ignored. Documents downloaded from browsers and WhatsApp are scattered, and users are not alerted when new files arrive. Many apps ask for broad access to photos and media, which raises privacy concerns. There is a clear need for a lightweight, AI-powered Android app that finds, prioritizes and opens documents quickly and respects privacy.\n\nSlide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE MY RESPONSIBILITIES The goal is to design and build a mobile app that helps users find, prioritize and access their documents easily. It works through AI natural-language search, priority tagging, an AI Vault for indexed documents, and simple, secure file permissions. Designing the app interface and navigation. Building file listing, search and priority modules. Developing the AI chat and AI Vault features. Adding notifications, themes and profile settings. Testing the app with users for smooth performance. Collecting feedback and improving the design.\n\nSlide 7: Project Plan Phase Wk 1 Wk 2 Wk 3 Wk 4 Wk 5 Wk 6 Concept Development & Research UI/UX Design & Prototyping Frontend Development AI & File Module Integration Usability Testing Launch & Feedback 28 Sep 5 Oct 12 Oct 19 Oct 19 Oct 26 Oct 26 Oct 2 Nov\n\nSlide 8: USER 1 TA Name: Tamil azahagan Age: 21 Occupation: MCA Student Location: Chennai GOAL : Tamil azahagan wants to open the right assignment or presentation within seconds, and to keep urgent files at the top. FRUSTRATION : His phone holds 150+ PDFs, slides and notes from many classes. Before a viva she spends 10+ minutes scrolling for one document. Important files look the same as old, unused ones. PROBLEM STATEMENT : Students need a way to search documents quickly and see which files matter most. IntelliFile helps through natural-language search, priority tags (Important / Normal / Low) and a Saved list for quick access.\n\nSlide 9: USER 2 VI Name: vinnoli Age: 26 Occupation: Software Engineer Location: Chennai GOAL : vinnoli wants to find any work document by describing it, and to be notified when new files are downloaded, without giving up privacy. FRUSTRATION : Documents arrive from email, browser and WhatsApp into different folders. He often misses deadlines because urgent files are hidden. He avoids apps that need access to his photos and media. PROBLEM STATEMENT : Working professionals need one place to see all documents, spot urgent ones and get alerts about new downloads. IntelliFile offers document-only access, new-document alerts, quiet hours and an AI Vault with insights.\n\nSlide 10: User Journey Map Persona : Tamilazahagan , 21, Student   |   Goal: To quickly find, prioritize and open documents on her phone. ACTION TASK LIST FEELING ADJECTIVE IMPROVEMENT OPPORTUNITIES Grant Access a. Open the app and allow document storage access. b. Read the privacy note. I feel safe and in control. Add a short onboarding walkthrough. Browse Files a. Open Files and view Device Files. b. Filter by PDF, DOC, PPT or Other. I feel organised. Faster loading for large libraries. Prioritize a. Mark files Important, Normal or Low. b. Check the priority dashboard. I feel in charge. Suggest priorities automatically. Ask the AI a. Type or speak a file name. b. Open the result. I feel impressed and saved time. Improve answers for vague queries. Use the AI Vault a. Move key documents into the vault. b. View AI Insights. I feel confident and informed. Richer summaries and deadline alerts.\n\nSlide 11: Competitive analysis Competitor Strengths Limitations IntelliFile’s Differentiator Files by Google Clean interface, fast cleanup tools and file sharing. No priority levels; search is mostly by file name. AI search plus Important / Normal / Low prioritization. Typical File Managers (ES, Solid) Powerful folder control and many file operations. Cluttered; no AI help or document ranking. Simple, document-focused layout with AI assistant. Google Drive Cloud storage with strong search. Needs uploads and internet; privacy concerns for local files. Works on local device files with document-only access. Cloud Note / Doc Apps Good for documents created inside the app. Do not manage files already on the device. Finds and prioritizes existing device and WhatsApp files.\n\nSlide 12: Business Potential IntelliFile AI targets anyone who handles many digital documents. Students (40%) and working professionals (30%) form the largest group, followed by small business owners (20%) and researchers or others (10%). These users need fast, reliable file access every day, which gives the app strong adoption potential. With AI search, priority tagging and a privacy-first approach, it can stand out from ordinary file managers. (Audience split shown is an estimate for presentation.)\n\nSlide 13: User Pain Points Time Wasted Searching: Scrolling through long file lists just to find one document wastes time, especially before exams, meetings and deadlines. No Sense of Priority: Urgent and unimportant files are mixed together, so users cannot tell what to open first and may miss deadlines. Scattered Downloads: Files from browsers and WhatsApp land in different folders, and users are not told when something new arrives. Privacy Worries: Many apps request access to photos and media. Users want an app that touches documents only.\n\nSlide 14: Flow Diagram Login / Sign Up Home Grant Document Access Files Device Files IntelliSpace Priority Dashboard AI Ask / Voice Search Open Result Chat History Saved Saved Files Priority Filter Open / Share Profile Edit Profile Theme · Notifications Help & Support\n\nSlide 15: App Screens: Files Priority Dashboard AI Document Vault Recent Files: Other Recent Files: PPT\n\nSlide 16: App Screens: AI & Saved IntelliFile AI Home AI File Search Results AI Chat History Saved Files by Priority\n\nSlide 17: App Screens: Profile & Settings Edit Profile Profile Picture Options Notifications Theme\n\nSlide 18: App Screens: Permissions & Support File Permissions About IntelliFile Help & Support Contact Support\n\nSlide 19: Usability Studies Round 1: Initial Study Participants: 5–7 users (students and working professionals) Search Issues: Some queries returned no match when file names were spelled differently. Low Clarity: Priority labels were not obvious at first. Navigation: Users wanted faster access to Saved files. Improvement: Add bottom tab bar and filter chips. Round 2: Refined Study Participants: 5–7 new users Improved Navigation: The bottom bar made switching tabs quick. Clear Priorities: Colour-coded tags helped users spot urgent files. Trust: The privacy note on File Permissions increased confidence. Final Recommendation: Add onboarding and smarter suggestions.\n\nSlide 20: List of Components Component Technology Specifications Mobile Application Android app Material-style interface with bottom navigation: Home, AI, Files, Saved, Profile. File Scanner Device storage access Reads documents only (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV, TXT) from Internal Storage and Downloads. AI Search Assistant Natural-language search + voice Finds files across Device Files and the AI Vault and keeps chat history. AI Document Vault Indexing and AI analysis Stores selected documents as indexed items and offers AI Insights. Priority Engine Tags and filters Marks files Important, Normal or Low; shows dashboard counts and saved list. Notification System Alerts + quiet hours Notifies on new downloads and silences alerts from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM.\n\nSlide 21: Project learning Project Impact What I Learnt IntelliFile AI makes it faster and less stressful to manage documents on a phone. AI search, priority tags and an AI Vault turn a long list of files into a clear, usable library, while the document-only permission model keeps personal data private. It can help students and professionals save time and avoid missing important files. Technological Innovation: Integrating AI search, file indexing and mobile UI into one app. Problem-Solving Skills: Handling permissions, large file lists, and priority logic. Impact of Technology: Seeing how AI and privacy-first design can improve everyday productivity.\n\nSlide 22: Product Design Patent PATENT Claim 1: A document management system that assigns Important, Normal or Low priority to files and displays priority counts in a dashboard and a filtered Saved list. Claim 2: An AI assistant that accepts typed or spoken natural-language queries and returns matching files from both device storage and an AI Vault. Claim 3: A privacy-first access model that reads only documents, indexes user-selected files into an AI Vault, and sends new-document alerts with automatic quiet hours.\n\nSlide 23: Next Steps Step A: Design Refinement Refine UI using usability feedback. Improve AI search for vague queries. Add onboarding walkthrough and more languages. Step B: Prototyping and Testing Build a high-fidelity prototype with full AI integration. Test on different Android devices. Run beta testing with real users. Step C: Documentation and Filing Prepare technical documentation for patent filing. Create user manual and onboarding guide. Finalise privacy policy and terms of service.\n\nSlide 24: Step D: Compliance and Approvals Google Play Approvals Follow Google Play policies for storage and file access permissions. Use Material Design guidelines for consistent UI/UX. Test on multiple Android versions and screen sizes. Publish clear privacy policy and terms before submission. Prepare app name, screenshots, description and category. Privacy, Quality and Security Data Privacy: Handle documents securely and follow applicable privacy laws. Access Control: Keep to document-only access with explicit consent. Security Testing: Third-party testing of AI Vault and storage handling. Reliability: Regular updates to meet store policies.\n\nSlide 25: THANK YOU E-mail: kishoreraja437@gmail.com Name:R . Kishore Reg No: 252524002','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-24 07:12:36','READY','IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R. AI Vault: Index selected documents for AI analysis and insights. Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.','[\"Slide\",\"Files\",\"Vault\",\"Intellifile\",\"Important\"]','[\"Finding the right file on time is slow, and important files get buried.\",\"AI Prioritization: Mark documents Important, Normal or Low.\",\"Important documents (IDs, policies, assignments) get lost among 100+ other files.\",\"Slide 5: Problem Statement Existing file managers list documents only by name and date, so finding the right file in 100+ documents takes too long.\",\"Slide 16: App Screens: AI & Saved IntelliFile AI Home AI File Search Results AI Chat History Saved Files by Priority\",\"Notification System Alerts + quiet hours Notifies on new downloads and silences alerts from 10:00 PM to 7:00 AM.\",\"Slide 22: Product Design Patent PATENT Claim 1: A document management system that assigns Important, Normal or Low priority to files and displays priority counts in a dashboard and a filtered Saved list.\",\"Claim 3: A privacy-first access model that reads only documents, indexes user-selected files into an AI Vault, and sends new-document alerts with automatic quiet hours.\"]','[\"Slide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date.\",\"Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists.\",\"Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents.\",\"Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.\",\"Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data.\",\"Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters.\",\"Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\"]','[\"Slide 2: PRODUCT PROBLEM Phones hold hundreds of documents, but most file managers only list them by name and date.\",\"Slow Search: Users must remember exact file names or scroll through long lists.\",\"Missed Deadlines: Nothing reminds users about time-sensitive documents.\",\"Slide 3: Project Overview THE PROBLEM SOLUTION Files are spread across Downloads, WhatsApp and browser folders, so search by name often fails.\",\"Users worry about privacy when apps read photos, media and personal data.\",\"Files are grouped by priority with a dashboard, saved list and filters.\",\"Alerts for new downloads, with quiet hours, keep users updated.\"]','[\"AI — Slide 1: INTELLIFILE AI Find.\",\"BY — IntelliFile is an AI-powered mobile document application BY Name : R.\",\"BSC — KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\",\"AIDS — KISHORE Reg no : 252524002 Department :BSC.AIDS\",\"XLSX — It scans documents on the device (PDF, DOC, PPT, XLSX, CSV and more), shows them in one organised place, and lets users search with plain la\",\"MY — Slide 6: Project Scope MY ROLE MY RESPONSIBILITIES The goal is to design and build a mobile app that helps users find, prioritize and access\"]','Kishore Reg No: 252524002',NULL,'2026-11-25 12:30:01'),(60,18,'IntelliFile_Project_Document.docx','DOCX','20.3 KB','uploads/documents/cc00dd74bd47b23e12eba375_IntelliFile_Project_Document.docx','Document','/storage/emulated/0/Android/media/com.whatsapp/WhatsApp/Media/WhatsApp Documents/IntelliFile_Project',NULL,0,0,1,'INTELLIFILE — AI-BASED INTELLIGENT DOCUMENT PRIORITY SYSTEM\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nAPP OVERVIEW: IntelliFile is an intelligent document management application that uses AI to automatically read, classify, and prioritize documents so that users always know which file needs attention first. Users can upload or scan documents such as invoices, contracts, notices, certificates, reports, and assignments. The system extracts key details like deadlines, amounts, and keywords, assigns a priority level (High, Medium, or Low), and presents a smart priority dashboard with reminders. Special focus is given to students, working professionals, and small businesses who handle large volumes of documents without dedicated document management staff.\nMARKET RELEVANCE: Individuals and organizations now receive documents through email, messaging apps, cloud drives, and paper, creating information overload. Important files are often buried among unimportant ones, leading to missed deadlines, delayed payments, and wasted search time. Existing storage tools save files but do not understand them. AI-driven document intelligence offers an affordable, scalable, and time-saving solution, making this application highly relevant in the modern digital workplace.\nPROBLEM IT AIMS TO SOLVE:\nInformation overload from too many documents: Users receive large numbers of files daily and cannot quickly identify which ones are urgent or important.\nMissed deadlines and delayed actions: Due dates hidden inside documents are easily overlooked, causing late payments, missed submissions, and lost opportunities.\nManual sorting and organization is time-consuming: Naming, tagging, and arranging files into folders takes significant effort and is often done inconsistently.\nScattered documents across multiple platforms: Files are spread across email, messaging apps, cloud storage, and phone galleries, making it hard to see everything in one place.\nNo intelligent understanding of document content: Traditional storage tools treat all files equally and cannot identify urgency, importance, or required action.\nLack of context-based prioritization and reminders: Priority differs for every user, role, and situation, but existing tools offer only generic or manual flags.\nINTRODUCTION:\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: Modern users handle hundreds of documents, yet most tools only store them without understanding their content or urgency. Priority decisions are made manually, which is slow, inconsistent, and error-prone. As a result, critical documents are delayed or missed while less important files receive attention.\nPURPOSE: The purpose of this application is to provide an AI-powered document priority system that automatically understands document content, ranks documents by importance and urgency, and delivers timely alerts, reducing the time and effort spent on manual sorting and searching.\nSCOPE: The application focuses on document upload and scanning, AI-based text extraction and classification, intelligent priority scoring, deadline tracking, and smart search. It is designed for students, professionals, small businesses, and administrative teams who manage large volumes of documents.\nGPCU\nG – Gap Analysis\nNo automatic prioritization of documents: Existing storage tools list files by name or date and cannot tell which document is most urgent or important.\nDeadlines hidden inside documents: Important dates and amounts remain buried in the text and are not converted into alerts or reminders.\nTime wasted on manual organization: Users spend hours sorting, renaming, and searching for files because there is no automatic classification.\nScattered and duplicate files: Documents spread across platforms and repeated copies create confusion and clutter.\nLack of personalized prioritization: Generic rules do not adapt to the user’s role, habits, and changing priorities.\nP – Product (App)\nSmart document upload and scanning: Users can upload files or scan paper documents with the phone camera, with OCR converting images into searchable text.\nAI-based classification and information extraction: AI identifies the document type (invoice, contract, notice, certificate, etc.) and extracts deadlines, amounts, names, and keywords.\nIntelligent priority scoring: Each document receives a High, Medium, or Low priority score based on urgency, content, document type, and user context, with a short explanation.\nSmart alerts and reminders: The system sends timely notifications for upcoming deadlines and high-priority documents that need action.\nPriority dashboard and smart search: A unified dashboard displays documents ranked by priority, with search by content, type, date, or keyword.\nC – Competition Analysis:\nCompetitor\nType\nLocation\nProduct Offering\nPrice\nBusiness Size\nTarget Audience\nUnique Value Proposition\nManual Filing & Folder Organization\nIndirect\nLocal\nPhysical files, or manually created folders and naming systems on a phone or computer\nLow\nSmall\nIndividuals, students and small offices\nSimple, familiar and no extra cost\nCloud Storage Platforms\nDirect\nGlobal\nOnline storage, folder sync, search and file sharing\nLow to Medium\nLarge\nIndividuals, students and professionals\nAnywhere access and easy sharing\nEnterprise Document Management Systems\nDirect\nGlobal\nWorkflow, version control, approvals and archiving for organizations\nHigh\nLarge\nLarge companies and institutions\nStructured workflows and compliance controls\nEmail Filters & Task Manager Apps\nIndirect\nGlobal\nRule-based labels, flags and to-do lists for documents and attachments\nLow to Medium\nMedium\nWorking professionals and teams\nReminders and manual prioritization\nU – Uniqueness:\nAI-driven automatic prioritization: Ranks documents by understanding their content instead of relying on manual flags or folder names.\nExplainable priority results: Shows the reason for each priority, such as “Payment due in 2 days,” building user trust.\nDeadline extraction and smart reminders: Automatically detects dates and obligations inside documents and converts them into alerts.\nPersonalized learning: Adapts priority decisions over time based on user feedback, role, and behavior.\nOffline scanning and secure processing: Core scanning and viewing features work without continuous internet, with privacy-focused handling of sensitive files.\nFUTURE SCOPE\nMultilingual and regional language support: The system will read and prioritize documents written in multiple languages.\nEmail and messaging integration: Direct import of attachments from email and messaging platforms will bring all documents into one place.\nAutomatic summarization: AI will generate short summaries and key action points for long documents.\nTeam collaboration and workflow: Shared workspaces, task assignment, and approval flows will support teams and organizations.\nDuplicate and version detection: AI will detect similar or repeated documents and manage versions automatically.\nVoice assistant and natural language queries: Users will find documents by asking questions such as “Show my urgent bills this week.”\nWHY USERS WILL USE THIS APP EVEN AFTER TESTING IS DONE\nSaves time every day – Eliminates manual sorting and searching by automatically organizing and ranking documents.\nNever miss an important deadline – Provides timely alerts based on dates and obligations found inside documents.\nPersonalized priority experience – Learns from user feedback and adapts the ranking to individual needs and roles.\nAll documents in one place – Brings files from different sources into a single smart and searchable dashboard.\nReduced stress and improved productivity – Clear priority lists and progress indicators help users focus on what matters most.\nDESIGN AND ENGINEERING STANDARDS\nUser-Centered Design\nSimple and clean interface: The application uses an easy-to-understand layout with color-coded priority labels suitable for users of all technical levels.\nOne-tap upload and scan: Simple actions allow users to add documents quickly without complicated steps.\nAccessibility-friendly design: The system supports readable fonts, clear buttons, high contrast, and inclusive design for elderly and differently-abled users.\nSeparate user and admin dashboards: Dedicated dashboards provide personalized features for individual users and management tools for team administrators.\nSoftware Engineering Practices\nFlutter / Android with MVVM architecture: The app follows structured MVVM design for better maintainability and performance.\nPython backend services: Python (FastAPI) handles authentication, database, AI/NLP processing, and notifications for reliable backend support.\nSecure RESTful API communication: All data exchange is protected using secure HTTPS-based API communication.\nModular and scalable application design: The system is built in modules (OCR, classification, priority engine, notifications), allowing easy upgrades and future feature expansion.\nDATA SECURITY & PRIVACY\nSecure data encryption – User credentials and documents are protected using AES-256 encryption for storage and TLS encryption during data transmission.\nSecure authentication system – Authentication is handled through Firebase Authentication with JWT-based session management to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nPrivacy and data compliance – The system follows GDPR-based data protection principles, including user consent, secure data handling, and activity logging.\nRole-based access control (RBAC) – Only authorized users and team members with granted permissions can view, edit, or share specific documents.\nProtected document storage – Uploaded files and extracted data are stored securely with limited retention, audit trails, and strict privacy controls to safeguard confidentiality.\nPERFORMANCE STANDARDS\nFast AI processing – Optimized OCR, NLP models, and API calls ensure quick document analysis and priority scoring after upload.\nOffline data caching – Caching techniques allow users to access documents, priority lists, and reminders even without continuous internet connectivity.\nTimely push notifications – Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) delivers deadline reminders and high-priority alerts on time.\nOptimized file handling – Compression and efficient storage maintain document quality while improving speed and reducing data usage.\nEfficient battery management – The application is optimized to minimize battery consumption during camera scanning and background processing.\nTESTING AND QUALITY ASSURANCE\nComprehensive functional testing – Unit testing, integration testing, and UI testing ensure stability across core features such as login, document upload, and priority dashboard.\nAutomated CI/CD testing pipeline – Continuous integration and deployment pipelines automatically test and validate system updates for reliability and performance.\nCross-device compatibility testing – The application is tested across multiple Android and iOS devices to ensure smooth performance on different screen sizes and OS versions.\nScalability and load testing – Load testing validates system performance under increasing users and simultaneous document processing requests.\nAI accuracy testing – Accuracy tests verify OCR quality, document classification, information extraction, and priority scoring against labeled sample documents.\nINTEROPERABILITY STANDARDS\nDocument import/export – Users can import and export documents in PDF, DOCX, JPG/PNG, and CSV report formats for easy sharing and record keeping.\nCloud storage and email integration – The system supports connection with cloud drives and email attachments to collect documents from multiple sources.\nCalendar integration – Extracted deadlines can be synced with calendar applications using standard formats such as iCalendar (.ics).\nETHICAL & TRANSPARENCY STANDARDS\nTransparent AI operation – Users are clearly informed about how AI reads documents, assigns priority, and stores their data, with a visible reason for every priority score.\nUser consent and data permission – In-app consent forms ensure users provide explicit approval before documents are scanned, analyzed, or shared.\nStrict data privacy protection – User documents are never shared with third parties or used to train models without clear permission.\nHuman control over decisions – Users can always review and override AI priority decisions, ensuring the system assists rather than replaces human judgment.\nRELEVANT STANDARDS\nSafety Standards\nISO/IEC 27001 – Information Security Management – Provides guidelines for protecting sensitive information such as personal documents, financial records, and contracts. It ensures secure storage, encryption, and controlled access within the application.\nISO 15489 – Records Management – Defines principles for creating, capturing, classifying, and managing records, supporting reliable organization, retention, and retrieval of documents.\nISO/IEC 23053 – AI System Framework – Supports the design and governance of machine-learning-based systems. It ensures that classification and priority algorithms operate reliably, transparently, and safely.\nISO/IEC 42001 – AI Management System – Provides requirements for responsible management of AI systems, covering risk assessment, accountability, and continuous improvement of the priority engine.\nData Privacy & Security Standards\nGDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) – Ensures that user documents and personal information are collected, stored, and processed with proper user consent and transparency.\nISO/IEC 27701 – Privacy Information Management – Extends ISO 27001 by adding privacy controls for managing sensitive document content and personal information within the system.\nDPDP Act 2023 (India) – Digital Personal Data Protection – Sets rules for lawful processing, consent, and protection of personal data of users in India, guiding how the application handles uploaded documents.\nSoftware & Mobile Application Quality Standards\nISO/IEC 25010 – Software Quality Model – Defines quality attributes such as reliability, usability, performance efficiency, security, and maintainability. This ensures the application provides a stable and effective document platform.\nISO/IEC 29119 – Software Testing Standard – Provides structured guidelines for software testing processes including unit, integration, and system testing to ensure accurate analysis and reliable application performance.\nIEEE 7000 – Ethical Considerations in System Design – Guides the responsible development of AI-driven systems. It ensures fairness, transparency, and ethical behavior when the AI evaluates documents and assigns priority.\nUsability & Accessibility Standards\nISO 9241-210 – Human-Centered Design for Interactive Systems – Ensures the application is designed based on user needs, improving usability and accessibility for people with varied technical skills.\nWCAG 2.1 – Web Content Accessibility Guidelines – Ensures accessible design features such as readable text, clear navigation, and compatibility with assistive technologies.\nISO 9241-11 – Usability Standard – Provides guidelines to ensure the application is easy to use, efficient, and effective for users managing and prioritizing documents.\n2D Design\n[Insert your hand-drawn 2D wireframe here]\nSuggested layout (four panels):\nUSER PROFILE — Name, Age, Phone No, Email, Role (Student / Professional / Business)\nAI ANALYSIS — Document analysis graph, Priority Score (e.g., 84%), Extracted Deadline\nDOCUMENTS — Upload File [Start], Scan Document [Start], Import from Email [Start]\nPRIORITY & ALERTS — High / Medium / Low list, Reminders, Report, Logout\n3D Design\n[Insert your 3D mockup image here]\nSuggested screens: User Profile • AI Document Analysis • Smart Upload & Scan • Priority Dashboard & Alerts\nFUNCTIONAL PROTOTYPE\nIdea Scanning & System Architecture Analysis\nUser onboarding and preference setup – Users register in the application and provide basic details such as role, document types handled, and priority preferences.\nAI-based document analysis and priority generation – The AI backend performs OCR, classifies each document, extracts key information, and automatically generates a priority score and suggested action.\nUser Authentication and Profiles\nSecure authentication system – Provides secure signup, login, and logout with encrypted sessions to ensure safe and reliable user access.\nUser profile management – Allows users to manage personal details such as age, role, notification preferences, and team membership (optional).\nDocument and profile upload – Users can upload profile photos and documents in multiple formats for analysis and organization.\nAI-BASED DOCUMENT PRIORITY MODULE\nDocument capture through mobile interface – Users upload files or scan paper documents with the phone camera for processing.\nAI content analysis – The AI evaluates document type, keywords, dates, amounts, sender, and urgency indicators for precise assessment.\nPriority scoring with explanation – Each document is labeled High, Medium, or Low with a clear reason, such as “Contract expires in 3 days.”\nReal-time suggestions – The system provides instant suggestions such as “Review today,” “Pay before due date,” or “Archive this file.”\nPERSONALIZED PRIORITY LEARNING\nAdaptive AI adjustment – The AI dynamically refines priority rules based on user feedback, corrections, and usage patterns.\nCustomized priority rules – Users can set custom rules, such as marking all documents from a specific sender or category as high priority.\nPROGRESS MONITORING & REPORTS\nVisual dashboard – Daily and weekly charts display pending, completed, and overdue documents by priority level.\nPerformance indicators – Counts of processed documents, deadlines met, and time saved are shown in a simple and understandable format.\nProductivity tracking – Visible progress charts and completion indicators encourage timely action on important documents.\nReport sharing capability – Document summaries and priority reports can be exported and shared with colleagues or supervisors.\nREMINDERS & MOTIVATION SYSTEM\nAutomated deadline reminders – Notifications alert users before due dates and when high-priority documents remain unattended.\nOn-time completion streak tracking – Tracks consecutive days of clearing priority documents to encourage discipline.\nAchievement badges and rewards – Rewards such as “7-Day Zero Overdue Streak” motivate users to stay organized.\nUTILITY & SETTINGS\nUser account controls – Includes Change Password, Edit Profile, Notifications, Logout, and Delete Account for full account management.\nSecure data handling – Ensures strong privacy protection, secure storage, and safe access to user documents and extracted data.\nTESTING AND VALIDATION OF PROTOTYPE\nStructured system workflow validation – The application follows a clear flow: Splash Screen → User Login → Document Upload/Scan → AI Analysis → Priority Dashboard → Admin Dashboard.\nReal-time AI analysis testing – OCR, classification, and priority scoring are validated through a secure API connection with the AI engine.\nUsability and accuracy validation – Testing confirms reliable text extraction, accurate priority results, and an easy-to-use interface suitable for all users.\nSystem reliability verification – Testing verifies system stability, alert delivery, and the effectiveness of personalized priority ranking.\nIMPACT OF PROTOTYPE\nBridging storage and intelligence – The AI-based system moves document handling from simple storage to intelligent understanding, helping users act on the right document at the right time.\nEmpowering productive document management – The system lets users manage documents independently while still allowing optional team sharing and oversight.\nImproving efficiency and accuracy – The prototype reduces time spent on sorting and searching, lowers the risk of missed deadlines, and improves decision-making through intelligent automation.\nCONCLUSION\nIntelliFile — AI-Based Intelligent Document Priority System is more than a basic document storage application — it functions as a smart digital assistant for document management. By providing AI-based content analysis, automatic prioritization, deadline detection, and continuous progress tracking, the system improves productivity, accuracy, and peace of mind. With its scalable AI-driven architecture and user-centered design, the platform has strong potential to expand into email integration, team workflows, and enterprise-grade intelligent document solutions, helping individuals and organizations manage information overload through advanced technology.','2026-11-25 07:00:01','2026-11-24 09:13:40','READY','INTELLIFILE — AI-BASED INTELLIGENT DOCUMENT PRIORITY SYSTEM\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nAPP OVERVIEW: IntelliFile is an intelligent document management application that uses AI to automatically read, classify, and prioritize documents so that users always know which file needs attention first. INTRODUCTION:\nPROBLEM STATEMENT: Modern users handle hundreds of documents, yet most tools only store them without understanding their content or urgency. PURPOSE: The purpose of this application is to provide an AI-powered document priority system that automatically understands document content, ranks documents by importance and urgen